WEBVTT

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.790
DMMO-RPG

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.540
Yggdrasil.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:04.460
A game released in the year 2126,

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.580
and now, after twelve years online,

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:09.770
the time has finally come for it to end.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:22.600
\"The Undead King\"

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.700
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.160
It sure has been a long time, Momonga-san.
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.590
To be honest, I didn't think you'd come, Herohero-san.
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:34.190
It's been about two years, huh?
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.830
Really? That long?

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.120
That's pretty bad.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.580
I've been working lots of overtime, so
my perception of time is all messed up.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.360
Isn't that pretty dangerous?
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.520
You mean for my body?
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.480
I think it's all messed up already.
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.330
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.620
I'm sorry.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.720
I ended up just complaining to you.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.010
Don't worry about it.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:58.260
Anyway, I think I'll get going.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.640
I'm a little sleepy.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.710
Rest well!

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.060
I'm really sorry.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:05.470
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.360
Momonga-san, it's been a pleasure.
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.630
Let's meet again sometime.
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.670
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:12.610
\"Herohero-san has logged out.\"
\"Great Tomb of Nazarick - 9th Floor - Round Table 8\"

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.250
This is the last day of service
for the Yggdrasil servers,

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:21.230
so I was thinking we should take the
opportunity and see it to the end.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.710
Let's meet again sometime, huh?

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:30.040
When and where would we meet, though?

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.830
Such nonsense!

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.090
Isn't this the Great Tomb of
Nazarick that we all built together?

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.190
How can they throw it away so easily?

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.350
No, I guess that's wrong.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.810
No one's betrayed me.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.540
That's right.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.900
Everyone's just caught up with life.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.610
Some even made their dreams come true.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.450
It can't be helped that they
chose reality instead.

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.620
\"Sebas Tian\"

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.050
So his name was Sebas.
\"Sebas Tian\"

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.350
And then we have the Pleiades battle maids.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:28.840
We had you guys guarding the throne room,

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.490
but in the end, not a single player got this far.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:39.140
I guess, as the guild leader,
I'll have them do some final work.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.520
\"Follow me.\"

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:50.360
I hope the other members will forgive
me for doing as I please, just for today.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:12.810
Albedo.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.520
The command was \"stand by\"?

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.750
What kind of settings did we have for her?

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:40.580
She supervises the guardians as the
strongest NPC of the Great Tomb of Nazarick.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.970
That's long!

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:46.970
Come to think of it, Albedo was created
by the settings maniac, Tabula-san.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.200
What's this?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.620
A slut?

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:55.310
So Tabula-san was a fan of contradictions?

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:59.070
But this goes way too far...

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.780
Normally I would need a special
tool, but as long as I have this...

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:08.730
\"She has perfect looks, but is a slut.\"

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.010
Should I add something?

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:13.850
\"She has perfect looks and loves Momonga deeply.\"

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:16.420
And she loves Momonga deeply.
\"She has perfect looks and loves Momonga deeply.\"

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.090
How embarrassing!

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.170
Am I an idiot?!

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:27.090
The command was...

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.240
\"On your knees\".

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.190
A relic of the past, huh?

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.390
That's me.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.830
Touch Me.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.710
Shijuuten Suzaku.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:49.570
Ankoro Mocchi Mocchi.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.110
Herohero.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.370
Peroroncino.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.980
Bukubukuchagama.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:56.010
Tabula Smaragdina.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.580
Bujin Takemikazuchi.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.130
Variable Talisman.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.590
Genjiro.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.590
Yeah. I had fun.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.140
I had a lot of fun.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.550
I have to wake up at four tomorrow.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:19.010
I'll go to bed as soon as the servers go down,

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:21.220
else, it'll affect my work.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:39.240
Did they delay the shutdown?

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:42.920
I can't see my menu?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.760
I can't call a GM with the chat either.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:47.930
What's going on?!

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.850
Is something wrong, Momonga-sama?

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:04.610
Momonga-sama?

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:10.240
Is there a problem?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:18.870
Huh?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.290
So the GM call isn't working, huh?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:25.970
Forgive me.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.460
Ignorant as I am,

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.300
I cannot answer your question
about this \"GM call.\"

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.420
Her mouth is moving?

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.470
There would be no greater
pleasure for me than

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.390
having the opportunity
to correct this blunder.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:41.850
An NPC is speaking to me?

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:44.360
No way.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.190
Isn't this some kind of error?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:55.680
The staff functions the same
as when I'm playing the game,

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.580
but I can't use the console.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.410
I can't contact the administrators either.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:00.790
What should I do?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.230
Sebas!

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.120
Yes!

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.460
Can I give him an order?

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:08.960
Whatever!

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.670
Sebas.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:14.340
Exit the Great Tomb and
check Nazarick's surroundings.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.450
Understood, Momonga-sama.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:23.520
The Pleiades will stand by on the 9th Floor
and guard the entrance for intruders.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.070
Understood, Momonga-sama.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:32.490
The NPCs understand orders that
aren't part of the regular commands?

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.040
What's going on?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:43.050
I definitely have to contact
the administrators.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:46.580
If I can't use the GM call, then
maybe I could send a message?

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:51.550
But would a magic skill used to contact
other players get through to a GM?

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:54.380
Can I even use magic in the first place?

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.720
Well then, Momonga-sama.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.970
What should I do?

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.080
I see.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.480
How about you come over here, next to me?

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:04.750
Yes!

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.110
She smells good.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.930
What?! Smell?!

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:13.360
There wasn't a smell function in Yggdrasil.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.610
Albedo. I'm going to touch you.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:16.500
Yes.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:21.240
She has... a pulse!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.660
Also, what's going on?!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.120
Why is an NPC ran by an AI reacting like this?

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:29.130
She almost looks as if she were alive!

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.390
Next is the final test.

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.630
This is the only thing I have to check!

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:38.630
Albedo! M-May I touch your chest?

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:39.260
Yes!

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.510
Th-This is completely necessary!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:45.520
That's right. As long as I ask her naturally!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.320
You really... don't mind at all?

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.610
I am so flustered!

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.070
Of course not!

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:53.110
Go ahead and do it as much as you'd like!

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:05.830
Let's assess the situation.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:11.340
The fact that I can do a mature action like
this shows that this isn't within Yggdrasil.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.260
The possibility that it's a
new DMMORPG is low, too.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:20.300
The only possibility is that this
fictional world became reality...

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.310
There's no way. But...

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:27.440
Talking to NPCs, them reacting
naturally, and having scents...

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.360
These are all things that would have
never been possible in this game so far.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.120
Anyway, how long am I
going to keep doing this?!

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:36.990
A-Albedo. Sorry about that.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:41.620
So this means you're going to
take me for the first time, right?

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.660
What should I do about my clothes?

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.780
Do you want me to take them off?

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:47.370
Or are you doing that yourself?

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.740
C-Calm down, Albedo!

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.130
This is not the time...

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:55.380
We don't have enough time to
be doing something like that.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.710
I-I'm very sorry!

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:02.600
It's okay, Albedo. I forgive you.

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:05.910
More importantly, I'd like
you to do something for me.

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.730
You can order me to do anything.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:11.790
Tell all guardians except for
those on the 4th and 8th Floors

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.730
to come to the battle arena on the 6th Floor.

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.490
Understood.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:22.110
\"Sixth Floor - Battle Arena\"

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:26.790
It worked.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:30.390
There's no problem with the
ring's teleportation function.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.330
I can use items, too.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.500
Albedo and the others are loyal
to me because of their settings.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:44.900
So where are the other NPCs?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:53.650
The twin dark elves that Chagama-san
created should be here...

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.260
Aura.

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:04.560
Welcome, Momonga-sama!

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:07.260
Welcome to the floor we guard!

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.370
Mare!

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.010
You're being rude to Momonga-sama.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:15.370
Just get down here already!

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:17.880
I-I can't do it, Onee-chan!

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.800
Mare!

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.350
A-Alright.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.310
Come on...

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:34.250
Hurry up!

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:35.550
Yes!

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.560
Geez...

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:40.570
S-Sorry for the wait, Momonga-sama.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:45.450
Okay. I'd like you two to help
me with something today.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:53.160
In Yggdrasil, you cast magic by clicking
on an icon that appears on screen.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.880
That doesn't appear anymore.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:13:01.010
But I can tell subconsciously
the range of my magic,

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:04.220
the cooldown time, and of course...

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:07.430
...how much mana I have inside of me as well!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.510
Summon!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:11.020
Primal Fire Elemental!

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:19.320
Amazing!

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.620
Primal Fire Elemental.

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.830
It's around level 80.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.250
Aura, do you want to fight it?

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:37.260
Is it okay?

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:40.860
I-I just remembered that I have
something to do right now.

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.460
Mare!

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.390
Primal Fire Elemental.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:52.930
Attack the twins!

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:04.900
Magic Shield!

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:15.040
Pretty easy, as expected.

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:18.540
I have no problems with my other
magic skills either. However...

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:20.570
Message.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:27.050
It won't connect to GM
members after all, huh?

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:30.860
Yes. What do you need, Momonga-sama?

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:34.130
The message connected?

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:35.270
Sebas?

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.190
How does it look on the outside?

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:43.210
The surroundings of the Great
Tomb of Nazarick are all grassland.

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:47.660
There are no buildings, humans or monsters

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.680
within one kilometer.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:54.200
The sky is as vast as that of the 6th Floor's...

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.420
A night sky?

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.820
Also, you said grassland and not a swamp.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:05.710
That means that Nazarick itself was
transported to a different location.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.470
So it would seem.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.970
Oh?

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:15.400
So I am the first?

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.970
Shalltear.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:21.740
She's the guardian of the 1st, 2nd and
3rd Floors of the Great Tomb of Nazarick,

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:23.270
and she's also a true vampire.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.860
My lord!

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:31.720
My one beloved lord that I cannot control.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:36.080
Shalltear, can't you give it a rest?

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:38.700
Oh, it's the brat.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:40.790
You were there?

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:47.050
It must be quite messy having
an insane sister like that, Mare.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.300
Fake breasts.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.620
Bullseye, huh?!

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:53.300
So that's why you decided
to use a gate to come here.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.840
Even though you were
in a rush to come here,

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:58.560
you still had to stuff your breasts.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.380
Shut your mouth!

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.870
You don't have any yourself!

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.700
I'm just 76, but you're an undead.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.040
It must be tough not
growing up at all anymore.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:11.640
Why don't you just settle
with what you have?

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.010
You bastard!

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:13.600
- You better watch your mouth!

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.200
- How nostalgic.
- You better watch your mouth!

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:18.310
Peroroncino-san, who created Shalltear,

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.170
and his older sister Bukubukuchagama-san,

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:22.210
who created Aura and Mare,

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.710
would always fight like this.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.460
It's so noisy here.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:30.690
You two are messing around too
much in front of our Master.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.760
Cocytus.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.830
He's the guardian of the 5th Floor.

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:38.010
His character is based around
the concept of a perfect warrior.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.520
So you came, Cocytus.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.630
I'll always come if you summon me.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.670
Indeed, good work.

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:49.780
Everyone, I'm sorry for the wait.

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.400
Demiurge.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:56.200
He is the guardian of the 7th Floor
of the Great Tomb of Nazarick.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:17:00.790
A demon in charge of leading
the NPCs in defensive strategies.

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:09.420
Well then, everyone.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:13.450
Let's proceed with the ritual of
loyalty to our Supreme Ruler.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:19.800
Guardian of the 1st, 2nd and 3rd
Floors, Shalltear Bloodfallen.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.520
I bow before you.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:25.310
Guardian of the 5th Floor, Cocytus.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.310
I bow before you.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.630
Guardian of the 6th Floor, Aura Bella Fiora.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:36.910
Likewise, guardian of the 6th
Floor as well, Mare Bella Fiora.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:39.200
We bow before you.

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:43.510
Guardian of the 7th Floor, Demiurge.

00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:45.080
I bow before you.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:48.250
Leader of the guardians, Albedo.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.430
I bow before you.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.280
Aside from the 4th Floor
guardian, Gargantua,

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:58.220
and the 8th Floor guardian, Victim,

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:03.220
all of the guardians have
come to bow before you.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:04.990
Supreme Ruler,

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.480
we await your orders.

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:12.110
We dedicate our loyalty to you.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.070
Raise your heads.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.530
What am I doing acting
all depressed like that?

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.600
You all came here when I called.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.660
I must thank you.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:27.780
You needn't waste your appreciation on us.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.790
We have dedicated our loyalty to you.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:34.550
I'm sure we're not enough
for you, Momonga-sama.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:41.680
However, as our ruler, we can only stand
before you and vow to work our hardest.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.560
We vow to do it!

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.810
I-I see...

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.540
I deeply understand all of your feelings now.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.860
I am confident you will remain loyal!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:52.900
Yes!

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.570
I'm tired.

00:18:58.090 --> 00:19:01.370
Those guys are serious about it.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.990
Th-That was really scary, right? Onee-chan.

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:10.840
For real! I thought he was going to squash us.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:12.750
I never imagined he'd be that powerful...

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:17.300
So that's Momonga-sama when
he shows himself as our ruler.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:18.260
You're right.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.640
Is something wrong, Shalltear?

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:23.390
What happened, Shalltear?

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:28.300
I got a bit too excited at
his amazing presence,

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:31.520
and now it seems like my
underwear is a bit of a mess.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:34.900
You slut!

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:41.570
We just received such a strong wave
of power from Momonga-sama!

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:45.330
A woman who doesn't get wet from that
must be faulty, you big-mouthed gorilla!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:48.000
You lamprey!

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:53.250
My figure was decided by the creators!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:56.670
The same goes for me, though!

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:03.000
Aura, I'll leave these feminine issues to you.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.330
Wait, Demiurge!

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:06.180
Are you trying to make this my problem?!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.880
I'll stop them if something happens.

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:13.520
Is this really worth fighting over?

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.360
Cocytus!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:21.990
I'm extremely interested in
the outcome, by the way.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:27.620
They might prove useful at least as
reinforcements for the future of Nazarick.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:29.620
Wh-What do you mean?

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:34.170
Every ruler must have a potential heir, right?

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.300
Momonga-sama decided to
stay behind until the end.

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:44.380
But we don't know if he might
leave like the others someday.

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:49.470
In that case, there should be someone
else we could pledge our loyalty to.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:54.480
S-So you're saying that one of them will be
responsible for Momonga-sama's successor?

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:58.160
Your words approach blasphemy.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:02.990
But don't you think that we could pledge our
loyalty to Momonga-sama's descendants?

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:06.620
That's respectable.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:08.910
No, it's wonderful!

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.100
What a wonderful outcome!

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.460
I'd be the uncle...

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.690
By the way, Mare.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:16.500
Why are you dressed like a girl?

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:20.500
Th-This is what
Bukubukuchagama-san chose for me.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:23.950
She said I am supposed
to be a boy and wear this,

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:27.890
and I don't think there's a
mistake about my gender.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:35.420
In that case, perhaps that's the
appropriate attire for boys in Nazarick.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:37.560
Well then, Cocytus.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.110
Come back to reality already.

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.060
This would be a good outcome.

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:43.660
It's definitely an outcome I can wish for.

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:45.660
I'm glad.

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:48.740
Albedo, Shalltear, are you still fighting?

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:52.120
The fight's over, what they're doing now is...

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:55.670
We're deciding who is going
to be the main empress.

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:59.070
Thinking that the person
who holds absolute power

00:21:59.070 --> 00:22:03.890
over Nazarick will have
just one wife is ridiculous.

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:06.890
However, there can only
be one main empress.

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:09.200
That's an extremely interesting topic,

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:12.010
but would you give us our orders first?

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.820
You're right.

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:17.770
Shalltear, we can discuss
this at length another day.

00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:19.770
No complaints from me.

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:23.860
Well then, let's discuss the plan for now.

00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:29.160
I only chose magic-based classes,

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:33.160
but at level 100, even I should have
enough strength to swing a sword.

00:22:33.500 --> 00:22:34.910
However,

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:42.500
I still can't equip any weapons or
tools that don't belong to my classes.

00:22:43.610 --> 00:22:46.810
I don't even know what this world is,

00:22:46.810 --> 00:22:50.730
but the NPCs all seem loyal to me.

00:22:50.730 --> 00:22:52.730
I don't have any friends or family.

00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:56.480
I go to work, come back home, sleep,
and then repeat it all in the morning.

00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:01.800
Do I really have to try to get
back to my original world?

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:04.110
Momonga-sama.

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:07.880
Create Greater Item!

00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:14.100
Narberal, I'm going out for a while.

00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:19.170
This is really tiring.

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:19.830
\"1st Floor - Great Tomb of Nazarick - Central Mausoleum\"

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:22.350
I can't use any magic in this armor,
\"1st Floor - Great Tomb of Nazarick - Central Mausoleum\"

00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:24.030
but I can make do with items instead.
\"1st Floor - Great Tomb of Nazarick - Central Mausoleum\"

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:24.670
but I can make do with items instead.

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:30.580
Momonga-sama.

00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:33.800
I never thought you'd
come here with no guards.

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.770
Especially in that armor.

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:37.560
H-How did he find out?

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:43.130
I guess the only people who can teleport inside
Nazarick is someone wearing a guild ring.

00:23:43.130 --> 00:23:44.570
So of course he'd know it was me.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:47.570
I'm investigating something
of a personal nature.

00:23:49.430 --> 00:23:50.820
So that's how it is.

00:23:52.020 --> 00:23:55.540
I think you have the keen
attention to detail befitting a ruler.

00:23:56.060 --> 00:23:56.880
What?

00:23:56.880 --> 00:23:59.040
I was just trying to go out for some fresh air!

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:05.040
However, I cannot overlook you going
outside without an ally by your side.

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:09.180
In that case, only one of
you may accompany me.

00:24:22.370 --> 00:24:23.310
What's this?

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:26.950
It's a real sky!

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:39.110
Fly!

00:25:02.520 --> 00:25:05.610
I never thought I'd be able
to see a clear night sky.

00:25:05.610 --> 00:25:10.360
I can hardly believe that
this is real, Blue Planet-san.

00:25:11.290 --> 00:25:15.230
They're sparkling like an
untouched box of jewels.

00:25:15.230 --> 00:25:21.660
The beauty of this world is like jewels
meant to adorn your sight, Momonga-sama.

00:25:22.370 --> 00:25:26.420
If you wish for it, the forces of
Nazarick will take it all for you.

00:25:28.680 --> 00:25:33.070
Even when we still don't know
what exists in this world?

00:25:33.700 --> 00:25:36.050
However, you're right.

00:25:36.050 --> 00:25:40.310
World domination might be fun.

00:25:42.240 --> 00:25:45.310
Well, it's not like I could do that, though.

00:25:45.310 --> 00:25:50.400
That aside, am I the only one who
got transported here from Yggdrasil?

00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:52.340
No one got my message,

00:25:52.340 --> 00:25:56.570
but maybe they were out of reach,
or the effects of magic changed.

00:25:57.010 --> 00:26:01.530
In that case, maybe if I spread the name
Ainz Ooal Gown all over the world...

00:26:13.170 --> 00:26:14.630
Chief Gazef!

00:26:39.760 --> 00:26:41.100
Vice-Chief.

00:26:41.100 --> 00:26:45.140
Take some men with you, and
guide the survivors to E-Rantel.

00:26:45.140 --> 00:26:45.750
Chief.

00:26:46.260 --> 00:26:47.500
What is it?

00:26:47.500 --> 00:26:53.890
The King's order was to investigate the culprits
behind the attack to the village and eliminate them.

00:26:54.510 --> 00:26:55.800
That's right.

00:26:55.800 --> 00:26:59.470
However, even if the enemy are
actually knights of the Baharuth Empire,

00:26:59.880 --> 00:27:02.830
we were only sent here with 50 other men.

00:27:02.830 --> 00:27:05.470
That's because this is a
confidential mission, right?

00:27:05.870 --> 00:27:07.510
It's because of the nobility.

00:27:09.630 --> 00:27:14.500
Even those closest to the King know that
if his most trusted soldiers were to fail,

00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:17.480
they could use that to attack him.

00:27:17.480 --> 00:27:18.700
How shallow.

00:27:18.700 --> 00:27:20.240
That's enough.

00:27:20.240 --> 00:27:22.430
You must have noticed already, Chief!

00:27:22.430 --> 00:27:24.120
This is clearly a trap.

00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:27.600
Instead of dividing our military forces here,

00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:30.250
let's all go together to E-Rantel.

00:27:30.890 --> 00:27:33.710
Even if we have to sacrifice some villagers,

00:27:33.710 --> 00:27:36.200
the blow to the kingdom from losing you,

00:27:36.200 --> 00:27:38.010
its mightiest swordsman, would be greater.

00:27:41.530 --> 00:27:43.820
I was born as a commoner.

00:27:44.560 --> 00:27:46.220
So was I.

00:27:46.220 --> 00:27:49.070
The life of a villager is a life alongside death.

00:27:49.070 --> 00:27:52.300
It's common to be attacked by monsters.

00:27:53.050 --> 00:27:54.230
That's right.

00:27:54.900 --> 00:28:00.380
Then, did you never hope that powerful
nobles or adventurers would help you?

00:28:01.180 --> 00:28:04.020
I'd be lying if I said I never hoped for it,

00:28:04.020 --> 00:28:05.990
but no one ever showed up.

00:28:07.160 --> 00:28:09.540
Then shouldn't we be the
ones to appear before them?

00:28:11.780 --> 00:28:15.110
The ones who appear in front of those
who know the meaning of danger.

00:28:16.070 --> 00:28:19.920
We will help out the weak and
look strong in front of them.

00:28:34.080 --> 00:28:38.390
If only I could figure out how to
use this Mirror of Remote Viewing,

00:28:38.390 --> 00:28:41.240
it would help me monitor
the surroundings of Nazarick.

00:28:48.600 --> 00:28:51.330
Congratulations, Momonga-sama.

00:28:51.330 --> 00:28:52.780
Thank you, Sebas.

00:28:52.780 --> 00:28:54.420
Sorry for making you stay here.

00:28:54.420 --> 00:28:57.660
Staying next to my Master
and following his orders,

00:28:57.660 --> 00:29:03.430
this is the entire reason for my existence,
entrusted to me by Touch Me-sama.

00:29:03.880 --> 00:29:05.330
I see.

00:29:05.330 --> 00:29:08.810
Alright then, let's look for
a place with some people.

00:29:11.640 --> 00:29:12.950
A festival?

00:29:14.600 --> 00:29:16.360
No, that's not it.

00:29:27.600 --> 00:29:29.570
They don't look like bandits.

00:29:41.710 --> 00:29:43.260
That's strange.

00:29:43.260 --> 00:29:45.300
If I had seen this before coming to this world,

00:29:45.300 --> 00:29:47.190
I would've fainted for sure.

00:29:47.190 --> 00:29:49.220
How can I watch it so calmly?

00:29:54.910 --> 00:29:56.980
What shall we do?

00:29:56.980 --> 00:29:58.510
Leave them.

00:29:59.300 --> 00:30:00.480
Understood.

00:30:03.910 --> 00:30:05.530
Touch-san?

00:30:06.090 --> 00:30:07.370
We got some points!

00:30:07.370 --> 00:30:09.120
Two more and we can change classes.

00:30:09.120 --> 00:30:10.740
Hurry up and finish him off.

00:30:12.120 --> 00:30:13.340
He's pretty bizarre.

00:30:13.340 --> 00:30:14.770
He's disgusting.

00:30:27.570 --> 00:30:29.350
Why did you save someone you don't know?

00:30:29.350 --> 00:30:33.040
Helping someone in trouble is logical!

00:30:33.040 --> 00:30:34.150
\"Justice is here\"
Helping someone in trouble is logical!

00:30:34.150 --> 00:30:36.020
\"Justice is here\"

00:30:44.070 --> 00:30:45.440
No matter what,

00:30:45.440 --> 00:30:50.280
I'm going to have to test
my strength in this world.

00:30:53.780 --> 00:30:54.660
Sebas.

00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:57.040
I'm going to this village.

00:30:57.040 --> 00:31:00.170
Raise the security level of
Nazarick to the maximum.

00:31:00.640 --> 00:31:01.500
Yes.

00:31:02.090 --> 00:31:05.520
Tell Albedo to come with me, fully armed.

00:31:05.520 --> 00:31:07.680
Next, get the reserve forces ready.

00:31:07.680 --> 00:31:13.720
Send forces with invisibility or
camouflage abilities to the village.

00:31:13.720 --> 00:31:15.350
Understood.

00:31:15.800 --> 00:31:18.850
Touch-san, I'll repay my debt from back then.

00:31:22.780 --> 00:31:23.790
Gate.

00:31:27.940 --> 00:31:28.740
Onee-chan.

00:31:31.750 --> 00:31:32.490
Nemu!

00:31:33.400 --> 00:31:36.020
Run away, Enri! Run away!

00:31:37.060 --> 00:31:38.860
Hurry up and go!

00:31:40.570 --> 00:31:44.090
I have to buy enough time
for Nemu to run away.

00:31:53.180 --> 00:31:54.680
What's that?!

00:32:08.220 --> 00:32:09.320
Grasp Heart!

00:32:18.080 --> 00:32:23.150
If humans in this world were immune
to my favorite 9th Tier undead magic,

00:32:23.150 --> 00:32:29.090
my only option would be to run away.

00:32:29.690 --> 00:32:30.800
A monster!

00:32:32.660 --> 00:32:35.880
I don't feel anything
after killing a person.

00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:41.020
It wasn't just my body, my mind
is no longer human either.

00:32:42.440 --> 00:32:44.230
I came all the way here.

00:32:44.230 --> 00:32:47.730
So I'll use you to test my abilities.

00:32:48.210 --> 00:32:49.940
Dragon Lightning.

00:32:56.350 --> 00:32:57.810
How weak.

00:32:57.810 --> 00:33:00.870
He died so easily from a 5th Tier spell.

00:33:04.030 --> 00:33:06.750
Mid-Tier Undead Creation: Death Knight.

00:33:13.890 --> 00:33:16.110
It reanimated his corpse?

00:33:16.110 --> 00:33:18.520
That's pretty different from Yggdrasil.

00:33:26.270 --> 00:33:27.910
Death Knight.

00:33:27.910 --> 00:33:30.440
Kill the knights attacking this village.

00:33:38.930 --> 00:33:43.530
Why is a defensive monster running
away from the one he should protect?

00:33:43.530 --> 00:33:45.630
Well, I did order it to attack.

00:33:47.850 --> 00:33:52.130
Forgive me, my preparations took some time.

00:33:52.480 --> 00:33:55.640
No, that was great timing, Albedo.

00:33:55.640 --> 00:33:57.770
Thank you very much.

00:33:57.770 --> 00:34:02.590
That aside, what are we going to
do with these lowly creatures?

00:34:02.590 --> 00:34:07.460
Our current enemy are those
armored people over there.

00:34:08.290 --> 00:34:10.280
Understood.

00:34:10.280 --> 00:34:12.210
You look injured.

00:34:13.510 --> 00:34:14.400
Drink this.

00:34:14.780 --> 00:34:15.910
Blood?

00:34:19.620 --> 00:34:20.840
I'll drink it!

00:34:20.840 --> 00:34:21.870
So leave my sister...

00:34:21.870 --> 00:34:23.090
Nee-chan, don't do it!

00:34:23.090 --> 00:34:24.270
- What's going on?
- Nemu, you stay quiet!

00:34:24.270 --> 00:34:26.150
- They don't trust me at all.
- Nemu, you stay quiet!

00:34:26.150 --> 00:34:28.080
What did I do wrong?

00:34:28.830 --> 00:34:31.260
You lowly creatures!

00:34:31.260 --> 00:34:32.730
W-Wait! Don't be hasty!

00:34:32.730 --> 00:34:34.210
Lower your weapon!

00:34:35.090 --> 00:34:36.470
Understood.

00:34:37.090 --> 00:34:38.980
This is a healing potion.

00:34:38.980 --> 00:34:40.560
Hurry up and drink it.

00:34:47.400 --> 00:34:48.230
No way.

00:34:48.230 --> 00:34:50.260
It doesn't hurt anymore, right?

00:34:50.260 --> 00:34:51.480
R-Right.

00:34:53.220 --> 00:34:56.280
Do you guys know what magic is?

00:34:56.280 --> 00:34:57.740
Yes.

00:34:57.740 --> 00:35:02.290
I have a pharmacist friend who visits
town occasionally, and he uses magic.

00:35:02.290 --> 00:35:03.640
I see.

00:35:03.640 --> 00:35:05.640
That makes things easier, then.

00:35:05.640 --> 00:35:07.790
I'm a Magic Caster.

00:35:08.730 --> 00:35:10.530
Anti-Life Cocoon.

00:35:10.530 --> 00:35:12.800
Wall of Protection from Arrows.

00:35:14.300 --> 00:35:16.900
I've cast some protection magic.

00:35:16.900 --> 00:35:19.300
You'll be safe as long as you stay there.

00:35:19.300 --> 00:35:22.180
Also, I'll give this to you just in case.

00:35:22.740 --> 00:35:27.600
If you blow them, an army of
goblins loyal to you will appear.

00:35:28.090 --> 00:35:31.280
You can use them to protect yourselves.

00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:32.110
E-Excuse me!

00:35:34.610 --> 00:35:37.400
Thank you very much for saving us!

00:35:38.100 --> 00:35:39.530
Thank you very much!

00:35:40.150 --> 00:35:41.530
Don't worry about it.

00:35:41.910 --> 00:35:44.540
Wh-What is your name?

00:35:45.150 --> 00:35:46.540
My name?

00:35:46.980 --> 00:35:50.040
Yeah... That's right.

00:35:50.860 --> 00:35:52.540
You need to remember my name.

00:35:53.470 --> 00:35:54.550
I am...

00:35:56.450 --> 00:35:58.730
...Ainz Ooal Gown!

00:36:38.010 --> 00:36:38.670
Shit!

00:36:39.780 --> 00:36:40.760
What?!

00:36:47.510 --> 00:36:50.240
He's only attacking people
who are running away?

00:36:50.240 --> 00:36:51.810
He's doing it for fun?!

00:36:51.810 --> 00:36:53.760
God. Please save us.

00:36:53.760 --> 00:36:54.490
God.

00:36:54.490 --> 00:36:55.880
Y-You bastards!

00:36:55.880 --> 00:36:57.860
Take down that monster!

00:36:57.860 --> 00:37:01.490
I wasn't born to die in a place like this!

00:37:01.490 --> 00:37:02.750
You bastards.

00:37:02.750 --> 00:37:05.700
Buy some time for me! Become my shields!

00:37:05.700 --> 00:37:06.990
Chief Belius...

00:37:16.280 --> 00:37:18.170
Money! I'll give you money.

00:37:18.170 --> 00:37:19.690
200 gold pieces!

00:37:19.690 --> 00:37:21.380
500 gold pieces!

00:37:22.860 --> 00:37:25.140
1,000 gold pieces!

00:37:36.610 --> 00:37:38.330
Save me!

00:37:38.330 --> 00:37:41.280
Please! I'll do anything!

00:37:44.650 --> 00:37:47.470
Money! I'll give you my money!

00:37:48.330 --> 00:37:49.800
Money!

00:37:53.930 --> 00:37:55.730
No! No! No!

00:37:55.730 --> 00:37:57.100
God...

00:37:57.100 --> 00:37:58.450
Calm down!

00:37:59.590 --> 00:38:00.640
We're retreating!

00:38:00.640 --> 00:38:03.110
Wait for my signal, and call
the horses and archers!

00:38:03.110 --> 00:38:04.840
The ones left behind will buy us time!

00:38:05.350 --> 00:38:07.350
Prepare the formation!

00:38:32.960 --> 00:38:34.210
Death Knight!

00:38:34.210 --> 00:38:35.540
That's enough.

00:38:47.930 --> 00:38:51.920
I saved the villagers, but I
was looking for information.

00:38:52.680 --> 00:38:54.780
If I remain ignorant in this world,

00:38:54.780 --> 00:38:58.250
it would become a blatant
weakness if I ever meet people

00:38:58.250 --> 00:39:00.330
more powerful or influential than me.

00:39:01.530 --> 00:39:04.620
The village chief and his
wife believed the story

00:39:04.620 --> 00:39:10.090
that I was a Magic Caster who was only focused
on research and knew nothing about the world.

00:39:10.090 --> 00:39:14.700
They told me everything
they knew about this world.

00:39:14.700 --> 00:39:15.660
However...

00:39:16.110 --> 00:39:21.840
Even though I'm wearing this
cursed jealousy mask that I got

00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:25.980
by logging into Yggdrasil on
Christmas Eve at a specific time,

00:39:25.980 --> 00:39:27.810
they still trust me.

00:39:27.810 --> 00:39:31.930
What kind of people are
this world's Magic Casters?

00:39:32.660 --> 00:39:34.910
This village, Carne Village and Nazarick

00:39:34.910 --> 00:39:35.890
\"Re-Estize Kingdom\"
This village, Carne Village and Nazarick

00:39:35.890 --> 00:39:38.900
\"Re-Estize Kingdom\"
are part of the Re-Estize Kingdom, apparently.

00:39:38.900 --> 00:39:39.590
\"Re-Estize Kingdom\"

00:39:39.590 --> 00:39:41.500
And right next to the huge mountain
range to the south is the Baharuth Empire.

00:39:41.500 --> 00:39:46.140
\"Baharuth Empire\"
And right next to the huge mountain
range to the south is the Baharuth Empire.

00:39:46.140 --> 00:39:46.800
And right next to the huge mountain
range to the south is the Baharuth Empire.

00:39:46.800 --> 00:39:48.130
Then there's the Slane Theocracy
located between both borders.

00:39:48.130 --> 00:39:52.610
\"Slane Theocracy\"
Then there's the Slane Theocracy
located between both borders.

00:39:52.610 --> 00:39:52.850
Then there's the Slane Theocracy
located between both borders.

00:39:54.430 --> 00:39:57.790
The closest city to the village is E-Rantel.

00:39:57.790 --> 00:40:02.600
Goblins, orcs, ogres and other
monsters appear nearby,

00:40:02.600 --> 00:40:04.880
but since there are also adventurers around,

00:40:04.880 --> 00:40:07.470
you should be fine if you don't
stray from the main road.

00:40:08.140 --> 00:40:09.220
Adventurers?

00:40:09.220 --> 00:40:13.530
They're people who defeat
monsters for a reward.

00:40:13.530 --> 00:40:17.980
There is a guild of adventurers
taking requests in E-Rantel.

00:40:18.690 --> 00:40:19.940
I see.

00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:24.690
It seems like I'm going to have
to spend some time in the city.

00:40:32.630 --> 00:40:38.290
With this, the information about Ainz Ooal
Gown saving the villagers will probably spread.

00:40:39.200 --> 00:40:44.120
If any other Yggdrasil players
came to this world as well,

00:40:44.120 --> 00:40:46.720
I'd like to help them out, if possible.

00:40:46.720 --> 00:40:48.050
In order to do that,

00:40:48.050 --> 00:40:50.050
I have to try not to
antagonize them too much,

00:40:50.050 --> 00:40:53.150
and avoid unnecessary slaughter.

00:40:53.150 --> 00:40:56.720
Also, I'll need a just cause for my actions.

00:40:56.720 --> 00:41:00.690
It would be good if I could get support
from another country somewhere...

00:41:01.790 --> 00:41:03.140
That's enough.

00:41:03.840 --> 00:41:05.920
We've done everything we had to do here.

00:41:05.920 --> 00:41:08.140
We're retreating, Albedo.

00:41:08.140 --> 00:41:09.690
Understood.

00:41:11.240 --> 00:41:13.390
What should we do, Chief?

00:41:13.390 --> 00:41:15.100
Do you have any ideas?

00:41:15.100 --> 00:41:17.620
Another problem, huh?

00:41:17.620 --> 00:41:20.330
Did something happen, Chief?

00:41:20.330 --> 00:41:22.000
Oh, Ainz-sama!

00:41:22.370 --> 00:41:26.500
Some knight-like figures
are coming to the village.

00:41:42.640 --> 00:41:47.620
I am the Re-Estize Kingdom's
Chief Warrior, Gazef Stronoff.

00:41:47.620 --> 00:41:52.080
In order to defeat the knights from
the empire that broke into this region,

00:41:52.080 --> 00:41:55.660
I've received orders from the
King to patrol these villages.

00:41:56.070 --> 00:41:58.080
The Kingdom's Chief Warrior...

00:41:58.770 --> 00:42:00.720
You're this village's chief, right?

00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:02.800
Who is that figure next to you?

00:42:02.800 --> 00:42:04.080
Introduce yourself.

00:42:04.850 --> 00:42:07.840
Nice to meet you, Chief Warrior.

00:42:08.280 --> 00:42:11.000
I'm Ainz Ooal Gown.

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:13.280
This village was being raided,

00:42:13.280 --> 00:42:16.010
so I used my skills as a Magic Caster to help.

00:42:20.560 --> 00:42:24.190
I can't thank you enough
for saving this village.

00:42:25.030 --> 00:42:26.190
Chief Warrior!

00:42:27.250 --> 00:42:31.440
Mysterious human figures have surrounded
the village and are approaching.

00:42:42.540 --> 00:42:46.700
Serving one of the six holy
scriptures of the Six Great Gods,

00:42:46.700 --> 00:42:51.360
Captain Nigun Grid Luin
of the Sunlight Scripture.

00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:52.600
Yes.

00:42:52.600 --> 00:42:55.510
The Re-Estize Kingdom's strongest warrior,

00:42:56.090 --> 00:42:59.010
Gazef Stronoff, needs to be eliminated.

00:43:01.680 --> 00:43:04.140
This item contains a hidden
miracle of the Gods.

00:43:04.910 --> 00:43:07.390
Use it when needed.

00:43:15.910 --> 00:43:17.110
The enemies have arrived.

00:43:17.110 --> 00:43:19.990
They've completely surrounded the village.

00:43:20.410 --> 00:43:22.870
What in the world are they?

00:43:23.600 --> 00:43:27.620
The only ones who could send this many
Magic Casters are the Slane Theocracy.

00:43:28.030 --> 00:43:31.850
Not to mention they're part of the special
unit directly controlled by the Head Priest.

00:43:31.850 --> 00:43:34.210
They're one of the six holy scriptures.

00:43:34.210 --> 00:43:37.300
Then they're the ones
who attacked the village...

00:43:37.880 --> 00:43:40.470
They were disguised as
knights from the empire,

00:43:40.470 --> 00:43:43.310
but I guess they were working
for the Slane Theocracy all along.

00:43:43.860 --> 00:43:45.440
As expected.

00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:48.190
Is this village that valuable to them?

00:43:48.780 --> 00:43:51.460
You don't have any ideas, Gown-dono?

00:43:51.460 --> 00:43:53.590
If they're not targeting anything in particular,

00:43:53.590 --> 00:43:54.940
then there's only one answer.

00:43:55.940 --> 00:43:59.870
It seems like you're being
targeted, Chief Warrior.

00:43:59.870 --> 00:44:01.570
This is really troublesome for me.

00:44:02.160 --> 00:44:06.000
I never would have expected that even
the Slane Theocracy would target me.

00:44:06.930 --> 00:44:10.370
But that's an Archangel Flame, huh?

00:44:11.070 --> 00:44:14.160
Why is an Yggdrasil monster here?

00:44:14.160 --> 00:44:15.840
Gown-dono.

00:44:16.240 --> 00:44:18.000
Would you please work for me?

00:44:18.810 --> 00:44:21.220
I'll give you any reward you request.

00:44:21.680 --> 00:44:23.720
I'm afraid I must decline your offer.

00:44:24.400 --> 00:44:25.580
I see.

00:44:26.380 --> 00:44:29.040
In that case, please take care, Gown-dono.

00:44:29.040 --> 00:44:32.150
I thank you again for saving this village.

00:44:35.070 --> 00:44:38.070
I am truly grateful.

00:44:38.670 --> 00:44:40.850
And I'm sorry if this is too selfish of me,

00:44:40.850 --> 00:44:43.950
but I want you to protect them again.

00:44:44.610 --> 00:44:48.900
I cannot give you anything
right now, but I beg you...

00:44:50.180 --> 00:44:53.220
You don't have to go that far.

00:44:53.220 --> 00:44:54.830
Understood.

00:44:54.830 --> 00:44:56.920
I'll definitely protect the villagers.

00:44:57.370 --> 00:45:01.180
I swear by my own name, Ainz Ooal Gown.

00:45:01.620 --> 00:45:04.050
In that case, I have nothing to worry about.

00:45:04.050 --> 00:45:07.430
I'll just move forward towards them.

00:45:07.960 --> 00:45:10.730
Then, please take this with you.

00:45:12.190 --> 00:45:14.250
Is that a gift from you?

00:45:14.250 --> 00:45:16.020
I'll gratefully accept it.

00:45:18.880 --> 00:45:19.610
Well then.

00:45:20.110 --> 00:45:21.560
I wish you luck.

00:45:29.940 --> 00:45:31.920
The first time I saw humans in this world,

00:45:31.920 --> 00:45:34.520
I thought they were mere insects.

00:45:34.520 --> 00:45:36.600
But the more I interact with them,

00:45:36.600 --> 00:45:39.990
the more I see them as small animals.

00:45:39.990 --> 00:45:45.430
Is that why you swore on your great name?

00:45:45.430 --> 00:45:47.220
Maybe that's it.

00:45:49.260 --> 00:45:51.350
We're attacking the enemy directly!

00:45:51.350 --> 00:45:55.700
Create an opening and lead
them away from the village!

00:45:55.700 --> 00:45:57.670
Just keep retreating like that.

00:45:57.670 --> 00:45:58.980
Don't mess up the timing.

00:45:59.330 --> 00:46:00.230
Understood!

00:46:00.590 --> 00:46:01.990
Let's go!

00:46:01.990 --> 00:46:05.480
We're slicing them up in half!

00:46:15.310 --> 00:46:16.210
Chief!

00:46:31.870 --> 00:46:32.890
I see.

00:46:34.890 --> 00:46:35.880
Martial Art.

00:46:38.500 --> 00:46:40.520
Focus Battle Aura!

00:46:50.080 --> 00:46:52.330
Anything can happen
when dealing with magic.

00:46:52.840 --> 00:46:54.080
Shit...

00:46:54.550 --> 00:46:57.330
But still, this is all according to plan.

00:46:58.070 --> 00:47:00.780
Gown-dono, I'm counting on you.

00:47:04.970 --> 00:47:06.810
- Stay by the Chief's side until the very end!

00:47:06.810 --> 00:47:07.690
- We'll be the ones protecting the kingdom!
- Stay by the Chief's side until the very end!

00:47:07.690 --> 00:47:09.350
- We'll be the ones protecting the kingdom!

00:47:10.540 --> 00:47:15.030
I told you to keep retreating
after leading the enemy away.

00:47:15.030 --> 00:47:16.480
You're all idiots...

00:47:17.470 --> 00:47:19.860
But also men I can be proud of.

00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:33.410
We're at an overwhelming
tactical disadvantage.

00:47:36.240 --> 00:47:39.540
In that case, we have to
target their commander.

00:47:43.660 --> 00:47:46.110
You're in my way!

00:47:48.210 --> 00:47:49.610
Martial Art...

00:47:49.610 --> 00:47:51.640
Sixfold Slash of Light.

00:47:55.140 --> 00:47:56.210
Martial Art...

00:47:56.210 --> 00:47:57.270
Instant Counter!

00:47:59.310 --> 00:48:00.310
Flow!

00:48:01.520 --> 00:48:02.910
Acceleration!

00:48:08.100 --> 00:48:09.030
We can do it!

00:48:09.030 --> 00:48:10.390
We can beat them!

00:48:12.350 --> 00:48:13.660
Good job.

00:48:14.080 --> 00:48:16.660
I can't believe you can use
that many techniques.

00:48:17.080 --> 00:48:19.750
But that's all you can do.

00:48:19.750 --> 00:48:22.040
Summon the next angels.

00:48:22.040 --> 00:48:24.920
Focus on Stronoff and use all your magic.

00:48:33.270 --> 00:48:34.930
This is bad.

00:48:38.940 --> 00:48:40.510
Onee-chan!

00:48:41.630 --> 00:48:43.660
It's alright, Nemu.

00:49:14.070 --> 00:49:15.590
Kill him.

00:49:15.590 --> 00:49:18.100
But don't let just one angel do it.

00:49:18.100 --> 00:49:20.850
Get the job done with several of them.

00:49:27.290 --> 00:49:33.360
Don't underestimate me!

00:49:36.290 --> 00:49:38.450
I'm this kingdom's Chief Warrior!

00:49:38.450 --> 00:49:41.690
I love this country and I will protect it.

00:49:41.690 --> 00:49:46.420
There's no way I'd lose to bastards
like you, who want to hurt it!

00:49:47.070 --> 00:49:52.080
It's you who are going to die here,
as you sink into your fantasy.

00:49:52.080 --> 00:49:56.750
Gazef Stronoff, what
can you do in that state?

00:49:56.750 --> 00:49:58.660
We're going to kill you,

00:49:58.660 --> 00:50:00.140
and then kill the villagers too.

00:50:00.640 --> 00:50:04.520
Stop resisting pointlessly and die quietly.

00:50:04.910 --> 00:50:08.520
I'll make it painless, as a final act of mercy.

00:50:10.930 --> 00:50:13.150
I think it's time to switch.

00:50:16.730 --> 00:50:17.910
This is...

00:50:19.060 --> 00:50:21.040
This is the village storage house.

00:50:21.700 --> 00:50:24.790
Ainz-sama built a barrier around it.

00:50:25.800 --> 00:50:26.790
Where's Gown-dono?

00:50:27.190 --> 00:50:32.950
Well, he suddenly vanished
and you appeared in his place.

00:50:39.410 --> 00:50:40.930
I see.

00:50:53.040 --> 00:50:54.150
Who are you?

00:50:55.130 --> 00:50:58.660
Nice to meet you, people
from the Slane Theocracy.

00:50:59.420 --> 00:51:02.660
My name is Ainz Ooal Gown.

00:51:03.320 --> 00:51:06.670
But I would prefer it if
you just called me Ainz.

00:51:12.910 --> 00:51:16.050
I have some attachment
to that village, you see.

00:51:16.490 --> 00:51:19.180
So did you come here to
beg for the villagers' lives?

00:51:19.760 --> 00:51:20.680
No, no.

00:51:21.640 --> 00:51:22.640
To be honest,

00:51:24.820 --> 00:51:28.790
I was listening to your conversation
with the Chief Warrior.

00:51:28.790 --> 00:51:31.070
How very brave of you.

00:51:32.390 --> 00:51:39.270
You announced that you were going to
murder all the villagers I bothered saving.

00:51:39.270 --> 00:51:42.030
I can't imagine a bigger insult than that.

00:51:43.080 --> 00:51:46.550
An insult?! You sure talk big, Magic Caster!

00:51:46.550 --> 00:51:48.420
So what about it?

00:51:48.790 --> 00:51:52.430
Just offer your life to me without resisting.

00:51:52.430 --> 00:51:54.170
If you do, I'll spare you a painful death.

00:51:54.900 --> 00:51:57.580
But if you refuse...

00:51:57.580 --> 00:52:03.680
I'll have you die painfully,
drowning in your own stupidity.

00:52:04.820 --> 00:52:06.430
All angels, attack him!

00:52:11.620 --> 00:52:13.320
What a pathetic creature.

00:52:13.320 --> 00:52:15.740
This is what you get for
bluffing your way here.

00:52:19.070 --> 00:52:20.760
I told you.

00:52:20.760 --> 00:52:24.120
\"Offer your life to me without resisting.\"

00:52:24.600 --> 00:52:28.370
You should take people's warnings seriously.

00:52:28.370 --> 00:52:29.290
Impossible!

00:52:29.290 --> 00:52:30.880
It has to be some kind of trick!

00:52:31.460 --> 00:52:33.760
High Tier Physical Immunity.

00:52:33.760 --> 00:52:38.840
Completely nullifies the attacks from low
level soldiers, monsters and weapons.

00:52:38.840 --> 00:52:41.060
It's a passive skill, though.

00:52:46.600 --> 00:52:50.940
Why are you guys using the
same magic from Yggdrasil

00:52:50.940 --> 00:52:53.340
and why do you have the same monsters?

00:52:53.340 --> 00:52:54.860
That's what I wanted to know...

00:52:55.790 --> 00:52:59.110
But I'll leave that aside for now.

00:52:59.540 --> 00:53:01.360
Now it's my turn.

00:53:01.720 --> 00:53:02.830
Here I come!

00:53:02.830 --> 00:53:04.450
Get ready for a massacre.

00:53:05.630 --> 00:53:09.120
All angels attack at once! Hurry!

00:53:09.120 --> 00:53:10.900
Albedo, stand back.

00:53:10.900 --> 00:53:12.000
Yes!

00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:14.050
Negative Burst!

00:53:18.880 --> 00:53:19.630
What?!

00:53:20.310 --> 00:53:23.100
I-Impossible...

00:53:23.100 --> 00:53:24.720
He's a monster!

00:53:25.220 --> 00:53:25.730
- Fire wall!

00:53:25.730 --> 00:53:26.850
- Shockwave!
- Fire wall!

00:53:26.850 --> 00:53:28.290
- Open Wounds!
- Blindness!

00:53:29.230 --> 00:53:30.720
Word of Curse!

00:53:31.440 --> 00:53:34.190
They're all using magic from Yggdrasil.

00:53:35.610 --> 00:53:39.280
Who taught you that magic?!

00:53:45.230 --> 00:53:46.910
What happened?

00:53:47.360 --> 00:53:48.860
Albedo.

00:53:48.860 --> 00:53:53.760
You should know that low level
physical attacks won't harm me.

00:53:53.760 --> 00:53:55.790
It wasn't worth intervening.

00:53:55.790 --> 00:53:58.070
Please wait, Ainz-sama.

00:53:58.070 --> 00:54:00.510
In order to attack a Supreme Being,

00:54:00.510 --> 00:54:03.950
there is a minimum level that must be met.

00:54:03.950 --> 00:54:06.300
I cannot allow such a puny attack to hit you.

00:54:07.900 --> 00:54:11.430
In that case, wouldn't all these
insects fail to meet that?

00:54:11.880 --> 00:54:12.520
Don't you agree?

00:54:13.710 --> 00:54:16.400
Principality Observation, attack!

00:54:28.100 --> 00:54:29.500
Good grief.

00:54:29.500 --> 00:54:31.600
I guess I'll take care of him.

00:54:31.600 --> 00:54:33.330
Hell Flame!

00:54:40.440 --> 00:54:43.300
With just... one attack?!

00:54:43.300 --> 00:54:45.320
That's impossible!

00:54:45.320 --> 00:54:48.800
A high level angel shouldn't be
destroyed with just one magic attack!

00:54:49.170 --> 00:54:50.180
Commander Nigun!

00:54:50.180 --> 00:54:51.600
What do we do?!

00:54:54.170 --> 00:54:57.360
We're going to summon the Supreme Angel!

00:54:58.180 --> 00:54:58.860
That's...

00:55:00.930 --> 00:55:03.130
A sealing crystal.

00:55:03.130 --> 00:55:05.730
So they even have items from Yggdrasil.

00:55:06.490 --> 00:55:09.940
Albedo, use your skill to protect me.

00:55:09.940 --> 00:55:10.790
Yes!

00:55:12.910 --> 00:55:14.050
Look at this!

00:55:14.050 --> 00:55:16.830
The form of the Supreme Angel!

00:55:16.830 --> 00:55:19.880
Dominion Authority!

00:55:30.810 --> 00:55:33.780
This angel is your trump card?

00:55:34.640 --> 00:55:36.240
That's right!

00:55:36.240 --> 00:55:40.770
I've concluded that your power is
enough for me to use this angel!

00:55:42.010 --> 00:55:44.280
I can't believe this...

00:55:45.270 --> 00:55:46.400
How worthless.

00:55:46.400 --> 00:55:47.240
What?

00:55:47.240 --> 00:55:51.490
I was on guard for this child's play?

00:55:51.940 --> 00:55:53.620
Child's play?

00:55:53.620 --> 00:55:55.250
What are you talking about?

00:55:56.480 --> 00:55:57.300
Th-There's no way.

00:55:57.300 --> 00:55:58.460
No, it's impossible!

00:55:59.020 --> 00:56:01.210
This creature can't be defeated
by any human power.

00:56:01.210 --> 00:56:02.840
You're bluffing!

00:56:03.330 --> 00:56:05.210
Use Holy Smite!

00:56:08.860 --> 00:56:12.470
This is 7th Tier magic
that no human can defy!

00:56:13.110 --> 00:56:17.850
You can taste this godly technique that
can even erase demons from existence!

00:56:27.880 --> 00:56:30.830
So this is what damage feels like?

00:56:30.830 --> 00:56:32.120
This is pain?

00:56:36.580 --> 00:56:39.960
You inferior creatures!

00:56:39.960 --> 00:56:41.380
You did that to Ainz-sama?!

00:56:41.380 --> 00:56:45.130
To the person I love so dearly!

00:56:45.130 --> 00:56:46.630
You made him feel pain!

00:56:46.630 --> 00:56:49.840
You should know your place, pieces of trash!

00:56:50.350 --> 00:56:52.460
Calm down, Albedo.

00:56:52.460 --> 00:56:54.400
But Ainz-sama!

00:56:54.400 --> 00:56:55.930
It's alright.

00:56:55.930 --> 00:56:58.110
Leaving the angel's
surprising weakness aside,

00:56:58.110 --> 00:57:01.580
it's all going according to plan.

00:57:02.860 --> 00:57:04.860
It's my turn now.

00:57:05.420 --> 00:57:06.860
Know despair!

00:57:07.600 --> 00:57:09.150
Black Hole!

00:57:20.030 --> 00:57:22.480
A power that surpasses even demons.

00:57:23.300 --> 00:57:25.710
What in the world are you?!

00:57:26.360 --> 00:57:29.310
I'm Ainz Ooal Gown.

00:57:29.310 --> 00:57:34.470
A name once so famous not a
single person had not heard of it.

00:57:35.290 --> 00:57:37.710
Enough playing around.

00:57:37.710 --> 00:57:39.770
W-Wait a minute, please!

00:57:39.770 --> 00:57:42.630
Ainz Ooal Gown-dono... no, Gown-sama!

00:57:42.630 --> 00:57:45.610
Spare us... at least spare me!

00:57:45.610 --> 00:57:47.620
If you at least spare my life,

00:57:47.620 --> 00:57:49.800
I'll grant you any favor you want!

00:57:49.800 --> 00:57:51.490
You're wrong.

00:57:52.650 --> 00:57:57.900
Inferior lifeforms like humans
should just bow their heads

00:57:57.900 --> 00:58:01.370
and thank him for taking their lives!

00:58:02.040 --> 00:58:05.380
Inferior lifeforms?

00:58:05.980 --> 00:58:08.130
If I'm not mistaken you said...

00:58:08.450 --> 00:58:12.470
\"Stop resisting pointlessly and die quietly.\"

00:58:12.470 --> 00:58:17.350
\"I'll make it painless as an act of mercy.\"

00:58:24.500 --> 00:58:30.110
Were my actions adequate
for the lord of Nazarick?

00:58:30.110 --> 00:58:31.600
Damn it!

00:58:31.600 --> 00:58:33.650
That was really exciting!

00:58:33.650 --> 00:58:35.360
What is it, Albedo?

00:58:36.630 --> 00:58:37.870
It's nothing.

00:58:37.870 --> 00:58:42.180
However, Ainz-sama, why
did you save that human?

00:58:42.180 --> 00:58:44.210
You even gave such an
important item to him.

00:58:44.790 --> 00:58:47.880
That was just a useless 500
yen gacha item, though.

00:58:48.380 --> 00:58:51.880
I could have gone there in your stead.

00:58:52.440 --> 00:58:56.100
I know just how strong
you are, and I trust you.

00:58:56.100 --> 00:58:59.820
However, ignorant about
this world as we are,

00:58:59.820 --> 00:59:03.890
we must always consider the possibility
of our enemies surpassing us.

00:59:04.370 --> 00:59:07.870
So you used that man as a sacrificial pawn!

00:59:07.870 --> 00:59:11.300
I believe that's the correct
way to use a human!

00:59:12.170 --> 00:59:17.640
However, wasn't taking a direct
blow from the angel a poor choice?

00:59:17.640 --> 00:59:19.290
You think so?

00:59:19.290 --> 00:59:22.060
Even knowing that you'd
come out unscathed.

00:59:22.060 --> 00:59:27.530
Is there any woman in the world who would
be okay seeing their loved one get attacked?!

00:59:27.530 --> 00:59:28.920
Y-You're right.

00:59:30.570 --> 00:59:33.070
Let's go back home!

00:59:33.070 --> 00:59:35.490
Yes, Ainz-sama!

00:59:37.410 --> 00:59:42.110
First of all, allow me to apologize
for acting all on my own.

00:59:42.110 --> 00:59:44.890
You can ask Albedo what happened.

00:59:45.580 --> 00:59:49.060
However, there's just one thing
I must say before anything else.

00:59:49.930 --> 00:59:51.650
Greater Break Item!

00:59:56.210 --> 00:59:58.160
I have changed my name.

00:59:58.920 --> 01:00:04.590
From now on, refer to me as Ainz Ooal Gown!

01:00:04.590 --> 01:00:06.470
You can call me just Ainz!

01:00:07.490 --> 01:00:10.210
If there are any objections,
stand up and be heard!

01:00:11.050 --> 01:00:13.240
We accept your great name.

01:00:13.240 --> 01:00:16.670
We pledge full loyalty to
our respectable leader.

01:00:17.400 --> 01:00:23.430
Hail Ainz Ooal Gown-sama!

01:00:23.770 --> 01:00:27.770
We'll devote our everything
to the Supreme Being.

01:00:27.770 --> 01:00:30.020
Oh great feared king!

01:00:30.480 --> 01:00:34.280
Every creature in this world
will know of your greatness!

01:00:35.300 --> 01:00:38.400
Oh our king, who rules over everything.

01:00:38.710 --> 01:00:40.350
The ruler of death.

01:00:40.350 --> 01:00:42.410
Glory to the overlord!

01:00:43.050 --> 01:00:45.280
I'll give one order to all of you.

01:00:45.280 --> 01:00:49.170
Make Ainz Ooal Gown an eternal legend!

01:00:50.500 --> 01:00:54.450
The land, the sky and the sea.

01:00:54.450 --> 01:00:59.430
We'll have every intelligent creature in this
world know the name Ainz Ooal Gown.

01:01:00.480 --> 01:01:04.150
In order to one day see my friends,
who might be in this world as well...

01:01:04.150 --> 01:01:06.190
In order to have that name reach them.

01:01:10.820 --> 01:01:12.470
Demiurge.

01:01:12.470 --> 01:01:15.900
Would you tell me what
Ainz-sama said to you?

01:01:16.980 --> 01:01:21.660
As Ainz-sama gazed at the
night sky, this is what he said:

01:01:22.440 --> 01:01:29.660
\"Perhaps the reason I came to this world is
to possess that untouched box of jewels.\"

01:01:30.650 --> 01:01:33.170
And in the end, this is what he said:

01:01:33.970 --> 01:01:38.420
\"World domination might be fun.\"

01:01:38.420 --> 01:01:39.840
Everyone.

01:01:39.840 --> 01:01:45.140
The final objective of the Great Tomb
of Nazarick is to present this world,

01:01:45.890 --> 01:01:48.890
this untouched box of jewels, to Ainz-sama!

01:01:55.540 --> 01:01:58.070
\"Fortress City - E-Rantel\"

01:01:58.770 --> 01:02:01.340
So this is E-Rantel, the fortress city?

01:02:02.370 --> 01:02:03.320
Ainz-sama.

01:02:03.880 --> 01:02:06.400
What are we doing here?

01:02:06.400 --> 01:02:11.830
We're undercover as two
inexperienced adventurers.

01:02:12.700 --> 01:02:16.040
We're currently at the
lowest rank, Copper Plate.

01:02:16.040 --> 01:02:19.240
By completing jobs, and
surpassing Mithril and Orichalcum,

01:02:19.240 --> 01:02:22.040
we'll gain the highest rank of Adamantite.

01:02:22.040 --> 01:02:25.600
Then we will have access to
lots of useful information.

01:02:26.170 --> 01:02:28.350
As expected of you, Ainz-sama!

01:02:28.350 --> 01:02:29.560
That's not it!

01:02:29.560 --> 01:02:31.760
My name in this city is Momon!

01:02:31.760 --> 01:02:36.110
And you're not the battle maid Narberal
Gamma from the Pleiades, but Nabe!

01:02:36.580 --> 01:02:39.030
Excuse me, Momon-sama!

01:02:39.030 --> 01:02:41.490
Just Momon. Without the honorific.

01:02:41.490 --> 01:02:44.110
We're novice adventurers, and partners.

01:02:45.050 --> 01:02:48.120
Understood. Momon...-san.

01:02:48.890 --> 01:02:51.040
Well, I guess that's fine too.

01:03:15.800 --> 01:03:16.940
A room?

01:03:16.940 --> 01:03:18.770
It's five bronze coins per night, each.

01:03:18.770 --> 01:03:19.670
As for the meals...

01:03:19.670 --> 01:03:21.550
I would like a room for two.

01:03:21.550 --> 01:03:23.090
We don't need any meals.

01:03:24.210 --> 01:03:26.600
You're a Copper Plate, huh?

01:03:26.600 --> 01:03:27.780
This place is a bit...

01:03:27.780 --> 01:03:31.400
We just registered ourselves at the guild.

01:03:33.510 --> 01:03:35.550
Seven bronze coins per night!

01:03:35.550 --> 01:03:36.790
And you have to pay upfront!

01:03:37.190 --> 01:03:38.710
That won't be a problem.

01:03:41.030 --> 01:03:43.040
The room is on the second floor at the back.

01:03:51.260 --> 01:03:52.740
Good grief.

01:03:55.760 --> 01:03:57.980
Hey, hey! That hurt!

01:03:57.980 --> 01:04:00.960
What are you going to do in exchange, huh?!

01:04:01.980 --> 01:04:03.470
Look at that!

01:04:03.470 --> 01:04:07.250
I guess I'll have that woman over
there kindly treat my wounds!

01:04:09.840 --> 01:04:11.770
No, no. Please forgive me.

01:04:11.770 --> 01:04:15.620
You just started talking like a stereotypical
nobody, so I just had to laugh.

01:04:19.790 --> 01:04:25.420
Someone like you is too weak
to even have fun playing with.

01:04:29.430 --> 01:04:30.800
So?

01:04:31.300 --> 01:04:32.810
What are you going to do now?

01:04:32.810 --> 01:04:35.550
Wasting time like this is completely stupid.

01:04:35.550 --> 01:04:37.390
In that case...

01:04:40.210 --> 01:04:42.030
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

01:04:42.030 --> 01:04:43.400
What do you think you're doing?!

01:04:44.000 --> 01:04:46.780
It's your fault my potion ended up shattering!

01:04:46.780 --> 01:04:48.030
Pay for it!

01:04:48.350 --> 01:04:50.020
Potion?

01:04:50.020 --> 01:04:51.160
I...

01:04:51.580 --> 01:04:56.380
I skipped meals and alcohol
to save money for it, little by little.

01:04:56.380 --> 01:04:57.400
And today...

01:04:57.400 --> 01:05:01.030
You just broke the potion I had bought today!

01:05:01.030 --> 01:05:04.050
Then why don't you have
these guys pay for it?

01:05:04.440 --> 01:05:06.670
One gold piece and ten silver pieces.

01:05:07.040 --> 01:05:10.430
Though you're always drinking,
so I doubt you can pay that much.

01:05:10.430 --> 01:05:13.960
You're wearing pretty good armor there.

01:05:13.960 --> 01:05:16.430
So you probably have a
few healing potions, right?

01:05:16.940 --> 01:05:19.390
I don't mind if you just give
me back the item itself.

01:05:19.390 --> 01:05:21.330
I do have some, but...

01:05:21.330 --> 01:05:23.280
W-Wait! Wait!

01:05:23.280 --> 01:05:24.360
Alright.

01:05:27.550 --> 01:05:29.200
A red potion?

01:05:29.200 --> 01:05:31.610
There should be no problem with this, right?

01:05:33.430 --> 01:05:34.490
Yeah.

01:05:34.490 --> 01:05:35.820
At least for now.

01:05:48.150 --> 01:05:49.970
Welcome.

01:05:51.440 --> 01:05:53.510
Nfirea Bareare-san?

01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:56.890
Yes. Do you need something from me?

01:05:57.430 --> 01:06:00.020
I'd like you to appraise something.

01:06:00.020 --> 01:06:02.520
\"E-Rantel - Adventurer's Guild\"

01:06:02.520 --> 01:06:05.520
Hey, his full plate armor is amazing, huh?

01:06:05.520 --> 01:06:06.940
How much does that cost?

01:06:06.940 --> 01:06:08.150
He is a Copper Plate...

01:06:08.150 --> 01:06:10.340
I'm sure he's just a rich kid anyway.

01:06:10.340 --> 01:06:12.660
Was that a present from daddy?

01:06:14.730 --> 01:06:15.910
I can't read this.

01:06:16.400 --> 01:06:19.160
Narberal can't read it at all, either.

01:06:23.520 --> 01:06:24.710
I'd like to take this one.

01:06:25.570 --> 01:06:27.330
I'm very sorry.

01:06:27.330 --> 01:06:30.520
You have to be a Mithril
Plate adventurer to take this.

01:06:30.520 --> 01:06:32.090
I know.

01:06:32.090 --> 01:06:33.840
That's why I brought it here.

01:06:34.540 --> 01:06:36.300
However, these are the rules, so...

01:06:38.370 --> 01:06:42.440
My partner is a third tier Magic Caster.

01:06:42.440 --> 01:06:43.720
Third tier?

01:06:43.720 --> 01:06:44.850
At that age?!

01:06:45.300 --> 01:06:48.610
And I am a warrior equal to her.

01:06:49.000 --> 01:06:53.110
We're looking for a job fitting for our skills.

01:06:53.860 --> 01:06:55.430
I'm very sorry.

01:06:55.430 --> 01:06:57.990
But I can't do that, since those are the rules.

01:06:59.120 --> 01:07:00.490
I see.

01:07:00.910 --> 01:07:02.980
Then there's nothing we can do about it.

01:07:02.980 --> 01:07:05.630
I'm sorry for being selfish.

01:07:06.070 --> 01:07:10.380
In that case, could you find the
hardest Copper Plate job for us?

01:07:10.880 --> 01:07:13.060
Alright, understood.

01:07:13.060 --> 01:07:15.290
Good! Manipulation successful!

01:07:15.290 --> 01:07:19.760
Then why don't you help us out with our job?

01:07:24.990 --> 01:07:26.690
Alright, let us introduce ourselves.

01:07:26.690 --> 01:07:30.940
I am the leader of the Swords
of Darkness, Peter Mauk.

01:07:30.940 --> 01:07:33.740
That over there is the
eyes and ears of the team.

01:07:33.740 --> 01:07:36.070
Lukrut Volve, a ranger.

01:07:36.400 --> 01:07:39.710
Then we have the healing magic
user and nature manipulation user,

01:07:39.710 --> 01:07:42.670
Dyne Woodwonder, a druid.

01:07:42.670 --> 01:07:44.460
Nice to meet you.

01:07:44.460 --> 01:07:50.400
And finally, we have the magic caster and the
brains of the team, Ninya the Spell Caster.

01:07:50.400 --> 01:07:51.870
Nice to meet you.

01:07:51.870 --> 01:07:55.510
However, Peter, can you stop calling
me by such an embarrassing name?

01:07:56.390 --> 01:07:57.840
Isn't it cool, though?

01:07:57.840 --> 01:07:59.850
This guy is a talent holder.

01:08:00.250 --> 01:08:02.300
Oh, a talent?

01:08:02.300 --> 01:08:06.020
Those are powers that people in
this world are born with, right?

01:08:06.020 --> 01:08:08.520
He has the talent of magical prowess.

01:08:08.520 --> 01:08:13.530
If I'm not mistaken, he can learn magic
that usually takes eight years in only four.

01:08:13.530 --> 01:08:15.030
That's amazing.

01:08:15.030 --> 01:08:18.880
I think I was very lucky to
be born with that power.

01:08:18.880 --> 01:08:21.860
It allowed me to take one
big step towards my dream.

01:08:21.860 --> 01:08:26.540
Leaving that aside, he's a
famous talent holder in the city.

01:08:26.540 --> 01:08:30.170
Well, there's someone even
more famous than me, though.

01:08:30.170 --> 01:08:31.920
You're talking about Bareare, huh?

01:08:32.590 --> 01:08:38.180
Nfirea Bareare is the grandson
of a well known pharmacist.

01:08:38.660 --> 01:08:43.640
His power makes it possible for
him to use all sorts of magic items.

01:08:43.640 --> 01:08:44.590
I see.

01:08:44.590 --> 01:08:46.610
That human sounds dangerous.

01:08:46.610 --> 01:08:47.690
I know.

01:08:47.690 --> 01:08:50.810
So, going back to our job this time.

01:08:50.810 --> 01:08:55.190
Our objective is to hunt down the monsters
terrorizing the surroundings of E-Rantel.

01:08:55.190 --> 01:08:57.530
A monster hunting expedition?

01:08:58.100 --> 01:09:00.370
Based on the monster's strength,

01:09:00.370 --> 01:09:03.800
we will receive monetary
compensation from the city.

01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:06.040
That's going to be our
reward this time around.

01:09:06.040 --> 01:09:09.920
I see, so it's similar to
getting dropped items, huh?

01:09:09.920 --> 01:09:11.310
What do you say?

01:09:11.310 --> 01:09:13.670
Are you going to help us?

01:09:14.120 --> 01:09:16.420
Yes. I'm counting on you.

01:09:19.680 --> 01:09:23.610
Since we're all armored
already, should we get going?

01:09:23.610 --> 01:09:24.430
Indeed.

01:09:24.430 --> 01:09:26.180
Momon-san.

01:09:27.730 --> 01:09:30.230
You have a special mission request.

01:09:30.690 --> 01:09:32.230
Whose request is it?

01:09:32.630 --> 01:09:34.480
Nfirea Bareare.

01:09:40.510 --> 01:09:42.840
Don't do anything without thinking!

01:09:42.840 --> 01:09:44.370
I'm very sorry.

01:09:44.930 --> 01:09:46.590
Try to have some restraint.

01:09:46.590 --> 01:09:48.500
Nice to meet you.

01:09:48.500 --> 01:09:50.750
I'm the one who made the request.

01:09:50.750 --> 01:09:52.500
I'm very sorry.

01:09:52.500 --> 01:09:56.130
I've already promised to
work on a different job.

01:09:56.130 --> 01:09:58.260
I am honored that you requested me, but...

01:09:58.260 --> 01:09:59.580
Momon-san!

01:09:59.580 --> 01:10:01.100
This is a personal request!

01:10:01.100 --> 01:10:02.750
You might be right.

01:10:02.750 --> 01:10:06.640
But even then, it's still natural that
I would take the job I accepted first.

01:10:08.140 --> 01:10:10.790
But still, a personal request...

01:10:10.790 --> 01:10:12.650
In that case, how about this?

01:10:13.050 --> 01:10:17.400
I'll make a decision after hearing
what Bareare-san has to say.

01:10:17.400 --> 01:10:19.900
I'm Nfirea Bareare.

01:10:20.460 --> 01:10:22.610
I work as a pharmacist in this city.

01:10:23.280 --> 01:10:27.990
I'm thinking of going near Carne
Village to gather some herbs this time.

01:10:28.360 --> 01:10:29.580
Carne Village?

01:10:29.580 --> 01:10:34.460
So I want you to guard me
and help me collect the herbs.

01:10:35.010 --> 01:10:36.460
To guard you, huh?

01:10:37.040 --> 01:10:39.160
That's kind of troublesome.

01:10:39.160 --> 01:10:42.220
I don't have any skills to guard a third party.

01:10:42.220 --> 01:10:43.620
The reward will be, as usual—

01:10:43.620 --> 01:10:45.140
Peter-san.

01:10:45.140 --> 01:10:47.830
Don't you feel like working for me?

01:10:47.830 --> 01:10:48.810
What do you mean?

01:10:49.530 --> 01:10:51.230
In order to guard someone,

01:10:51.230 --> 01:10:54.720
we're going to need a ranger like Lukrut-san.

01:10:54.720 --> 01:10:56.390
And since the setting is a forest,

01:10:56.390 --> 01:11:01.280
perhaps it would be useful to
have a druid like Dyne-san.

01:11:01.280 --> 01:11:02.080
Indeed.

01:11:02.080 --> 01:11:04.650
That's a good perspective, Master Momon.

01:11:04.650 --> 01:11:06.530
I don't have any problems either.

01:11:06.530 --> 01:11:08.540
Thank you very much for the request!

01:11:08.540 --> 01:11:11.160
I don't have any problems either.

01:11:11.500 --> 01:11:12.990
That's good.

01:11:12.990 --> 01:11:15.170
Well then, let me ask one final question.

01:11:15.170 --> 01:11:16.290
Yes?

01:11:16.650 --> 01:11:18.670
Why did you request me?

01:11:20.360 --> 01:11:23.600
I just arrived in town yesterday.

01:11:23.600 --> 01:11:27.850
I don't have any friends,
and no one knows who I am.

01:11:27.850 --> 01:11:29.810
So I want to know why.

01:11:30.760 --> 01:11:33.560
Actually, I heard about
the incident at the inn.

01:11:33.560 --> 01:11:35.310
The incident at the inn?

01:11:35.310 --> 01:11:36.560
Yes.

01:11:36.560 --> 01:11:40.270
I heard a rumor from a customer
that stopped by our shop

01:11:40.270 --> 01:11:43.190
about how you sent a high rank
adventurer flying just like that.

01:11:43.190 --> 01:11:47.670
And since the person I've been
requesting so far is in a different town,

01:11:47.670 --> 01:11:50.200
I thought this was a good
chance to find someone new.

01:11:50.200 --> 01:11:54.210
I also thought that a Copper Plate would
be cheaper than other adventurers.

01:11:55.100 --> 01:11:56.710
That's true.

01:11:57.650 --> 01:11:59.340
Any other questions?

01:11:59.340 --> 01:12:01.360
- No, we're ready to leave at any moment.

01:12:01.360 --> 01:12:02.260
- There's no way, though...
- No, we're ready to leave at any moment.

01:12:02.260 --> 01:12:03.530
- There's no way, though...
- Understood.

01:12:04.340 --> 01:12:07.130
Well then, shall we get going?

01:12:32.670 --> 01:12:33.990
Albedo.

01:12:37.240 --> 01:12:40.500
What are you doing in Ainz-sama's bedroom?

01:12:41.940 --> 01:12:47.630
I was thinking of letting Ainz-sama get
enveloped by my scent when he came back.

01:12:48.270 --> 01:12:52.680
Ainz-sama is an undead,
and has no need for sleep.

01:12:53.020 --> 01:12:55.470
Well, just take it easy, okay?

01:12:56.570 --> 01:13:00.210
I don't know what you're
talking about, but okay.

01:13:00.210 --> 01:13:02.340
Right? Ainz-sama?

01:13:05.840 --> 01:13:10.330
That's a body pillow?

01:13:10.330 --> 01:13:12.530
Yes. It's homemade.

01:13:13.180 --> 01:13:23.540
I'm also knitting socks and clothes for
our future child until they turn five.

01:13:24.000 --> 01:13:27.010
It doesn't matter if they're a boy or a girl.

01:13:28.810 --> 01:13:31.180
What if they're born with
both sexes, or neither?

01:13:31.730 --> 01:13:36.810
Apparently the Supreme Beings require young
boys to dress like girls and vice versa, though.

01:13:36.810 --> 01:13:40.190
That's good news!

01:13:40.190 --> 01:13:42.670
Thank you, Demiurge!

01:13:43.540 --> 01:13:44.150
- I have to think of the designs now!

01:13:44.150 --> 01:13:46.190
- You're welcome.
- I have to think of the designs now!

01:14:09.590 --> 01:14:10.720
Peter-san.

01:14:10.720 --> 01:14:11.820
Yes?

01:14:11.820 --> 01:14:14.210
Shall we take a break over there?

01:14:17.110 --> 01:14:18.560
Yeah, you're right.

01:14:19.330 --> 01:14:20.550
Momon-san.

01:14:22.040 --> 01:14:23.330
Alright.

01:14:30.950 --> 01:14:35.290
Momon-san, the area will get a
little dangerous from here on.

01:14:35.290 --> 01:14:36.690
Understood.

01:14:36.690 --> 01:14:37.910
I'll be careful.

01:14:37.910 --> 01:14:42.120
I think this is the Wise King of
the Forest's territory, right?

01:14:42.520 --> 01:14:45.130
The Wise King of the Forest?

01:14:45.130 --> 01:14:48.970
It's a powerful magical beast that
has lived for hundreds of years.

01:14:48.970 --> 01:14:53.860
Look out for a white four-legged
creature with the tail of a snake.

01:14:53.860 --> 01:14:57.720
It's very knowledgeable and it can use magic.

01:14:57.720 --> 01:15:01.480
I'd like to meet it someday.

01:15:05.900 --> 01:15:11.000
Nabe-chan, you always
look pretty carefree, right?

01:15:12.300 --> 01:15:15.020
That's because you believe
in my eyes and ears, right?

01:15:15.020 --> 01:15:16.830
Not because of you.

01:15:16.830 --> 01:15:18.900
It's because of Momon-san...

01:15:24.200 --> 01:15:28.250
Say. Are you sure you're not lovers?

01:15:28.960 --> 01:15:32.180
L-Lovers?! What are you talking about?!

01:15:32.180 --> 01:15:33.300
- Instead of me, he has a woman named Albedo-sama!

01:15:33.300 --> 01:15:34.880
- Hey! Wait, you!
- Instead of me, he has a woman named Albedo-sama!

01:15:35.680 --> 01:15:37.160
What are you saying?!

01:15:44.210 --> 01:15:45.550
Lukurt-san.

01:15:45.550 --> 01:15:47.860
Can we stop it with the personal questions?

01:15:47.860 --> 01:15:50.200
Ah, alright.

01:15:50.200 --> 01:15:52.990
So you already had
someone else, Momon-san.

01:15:52.990 --> 01:15:56.130
Momon-san, I'm sorry for my partner.

01:15:56.130 --> 01:15:59.120
Even though asking about each
other's personal lives is taboo.

01:15:59.560 --> 01:16:00.810
No, no.

01:16:00.810 --> 01:16:05.120
As long as it doesn't happen again, that's fine.

01:16:05.120 --> 01:16:08.630
You should really watch out, Lukurt—

01:16:09.860 --> 01:16:11.130
They're making their move.

01:16:13.150 --> 01:16:14.240
Where are they?

01:16:14.240 --> 01:16:15.470
Over there, over there.

01:16:24.480 --> 01:16:27.180
I guess we can't avoid fighting them, huh?

01:16:27.180 --> 01:16:31.540
Nfirea-san, please hide
yourself inside the cart.

01:16:31.540 --> 01:16:33.780
Yes. I'm counting on you.

01:16:34.110 --> 01:16:36.780
Momon-san, how are we
going to split our forces?

01:16:36.780 --> 01:16:40.020
Could you guys protect Nfirea-san?

01:16:40.020 --> 01:16:43.790
Let's show him how quickly
we can defeat them.

01:16:43.790 --> 01:16:45.450
Understood.

01:16:45.450 --> 01:16:49.040
That said, we'll give you
support as much as possible.

01:16:49.040 --> 01:16:50.800
If we fight like this,

01:16:50.800 --> 01:16:52.960
they might end up running into the forest.

01:16:52.960 --> 01:16:55.410
Then we should just do the same as always,

01:16:55.410 --> 01:16:57.970
bait them and then attack head-on.

01:16:57.970 --> 01:16:59.740
That sounds good.

01:16:59.740 --> 01:17:00.960
Also, Peter.

01:17:00.960 --> 01:17:04.040
Even if Momon-san blocks the enemy attacks,

01:17:04.040 --> 01:17:05.980
how will we deal with the stragglers?

01:17:06.370 --> 01:17:10.350
I will use the Fortress Martial
Art and take care of the ogres.

01:17:10.350 --> 01:17:12.140
Dyne, you take care of the goblins.

01:17:12.140 --> 01:17:13.730
Understood.

01:17:13.730 --> 01:17:15.770
Ninya, protect me with your defensive magic.

01:17:15.770 --> 01:17:19.340
And then, use your attack magic
as you see fit for the battle.

01:17:19.340 --> 01:17:20.740
Alright, understood.

01:17:20.740 --> 01:17:23.530
Lukurt, please hunt the goblins down.

01:17:23.530 --> 01:17:25.650
And if any ogres get through, block them!

01:17:25.650 --> 01:17:26.870
Leave it to me.

01:17:26.870 --> 01:17:28.930
Are you guys okay with that?

01:17:28.930 --> 01:17:29.950
Yes.

01:17:31.130 --> 01:17:33.130
First!

01:17:41.930 --> 01:17:43.400
They fell for it!

01:17:45.390 --> 01:17:47.980
Reinforce Armor!

01:17:48.890 --> 01:17:51.100
Twine Plant!

01:18:17.510 --> 01:18:19.030
Amazing...

01:18:19.030 --> 01:18:20.510
He's higher than Mithril.

01:18:20.930 --> 01:18:22.260
Orichalchum?!

01:18:22.260 --> 01:18:25.260
Don't tell me... Adamantite?!

01:18:26.390 --> 01:18:30.020
What? You're not charging at me?

01:18:40.740 --> 01:18:42.570
Alright then, what about the rest?

01:18:45.410 --> 01:18:47.120
They're coming here as well!

01:18:48.200 --> 01:18:49.380
Take this!

01:18:50.000 --> 01:18:51.330
Magic Arrow!

01:18:53.960 --> 01:18:56.260
Here they come!

01:18:56.260 --> 01:18:57.460
Let's go.

01:18:57.950 --> 01:18:59.590
They're a good party.

01:18:59.590 --> 01:19:02.970
They know their own strengths
and form a solid team.

01:19:03.370 --> 01:19:06.720
Though they're not as good
as my old teammates.

01:19:16.560 --> 01:19:18.130
Nabe, do it.

01:19:18.130 --> 01:19:19.070
Yes.

01:19:22.450 --> 01:19:24.100
Lightning!

01:19:29.910 --> 01:19:31.910
Run away! Run away!

01:19:33.240 --> 01:19:33.910
Wait!

01:19:33.910 --> 01:19:35.750
Don't let them escape!

01:19:40.550 --> 01:19:42.800
Light Healing.

01:19:47.630 --> 01:19:49.510
What are you doing?

01:19:49.510 --> 01:19:55.100
If you gather parts of the defeated
monsters, you can get a reward.

01:19:55.470 --> 01:19:59.480
So they don't drop any items
like crystals or anything?

01:19:59.480 --> 01:20:03.740
I've never heard of ogres
carrying items like crystals.

01:20:04.110 --> 01:20:05.370
I see.

01:20:12.550 --> 01:20:17.120
By the way, why are you called
the Swords of Darkness?

01:20:17.120 --> 01:20:18.750
Ah, that?

01:20:18.750 --> 01:20:22.000
A hero called the \"Black Knight\" who was

01:20:22.000 --> 01:20:26.130
part of the Thirteen Heroes
had four swords called that.

01:20:27.840 --> 01:20:32.970
Well, our objective is finding those swords.

01:20:33.460 --> 01:20:39.730
These will do until the day we
get our hands on the real ones.

01:20:40.830 --> 01:20:43.780
These may not be the four swords.

01:20:43.780 --> 01:20:49.370
But there is no doubt that these
represent the creation of our team.

01:20:49.370 --> 01:20:50.350
Yeah.

01:20:50.350 --> 01:20:53.870
Lukurt said something pretty good, for once.

01:20:53.870 --> 01:20:56.000
Hey, aren't you being cruel?!

01:20:56.000 --> 01:20:58.120
We have to praise you every now and then.

01:20:58.120 --> 01:21:01.150
You guys are too mean to me!

01:21:01.150 --> 01:21:03.000
I used to be like this as well.

01:21:04.120 --> 01:21:07.580
I went on adventures with
everyone, and collected materials...

01:21:07.580 --> 01:21:09.790
And that's how we built Nazarick.

01:21:11.110 --> 01:21:15.490
Do all adventurers get along like this?

01:21:15.490 --> 01:21:16.310
Yes.

01:21:16.310 --> 01:21:18.270
Our lives depend on each other, after all.

01:21:18.270 --> 01:21:21.520
Besides, our team is just guys.

01:21:21.520 --> 01:21:25.200
I've heard that girls can cause a lot of trouble.

01:21:25.200 --> 01:21:30.280
We have a pretty clear objective as a team.

01:21:30.630 --> 01:21:35.110
It's completely different when
everyone is focusing on the same thing.

01:21:35.110 --> 01:21:37.040
Did you have a team as well, Momon-san?

01:21:37.540 --> 01:21:41.430
We weren't adventurers, though.

01:21:42.760 --> 01:21:48.980
Long ago, a holy knight saved
me when I was weak and lonely.

01:21:49.700 --> 01:21:54.680
I followed him, and met the first
people I could ever call my partners.

01:21:56.330 --> 01:21:58.790
They were great companions.

01:21:58.790 --> 01:22:02.690
And they were my best friends as well.

01:22:03.140 --> 01:22:06.330
I'll never forget the days we spent together.

01:22:07.860 --> 01:22:09.950
Ainz Ooal Gown.

01:22:09.950 --> 01:22:12.150
It was my everything.

01:22:14.200 --> 01:22:15.450
Momon-san.

01:22:15.940 --> 01:22:20.080
Someday I'm sure you'll find
people as wonderful as them.

01:22:20.080 --> 01:22:22.080
That won't ever happen.

01:22:23.980 --> 01:22:25.080
Excuse me.

01:22:27.340 --> 01:22:29.930
Nabe, I'm going to eat over there.

01:22:29.930 --> 01:22:32.340
Allow me to join you, then.

01:22:33.060 --> 01:22:34.970
I see.

01:22:38.680 --> 01:22:40.980
Seems like I said something inappropriate.

01:22:40.980 --> 01:22:44.480
Yeah. Maybe something happened.

01:22:47.480 --> 01:22:50.760
Maybe they all got wiped out.

01:22:50.760 --> 01:22:56.330
People who have lost their entire
team sometimes act like that.

01:22:56.330 --> 01:22:59.460
That's a pretty hard topic to discuss.

01:23:00.080 --> 01:23:04.200
You can never take back
the words you've said.

01:23:04.200 --> 01:23:10.500
So instead, you can only overwrite
them with something new.

01:23:11.990 --> 01:23:13.540
I'll do that.

01:23:16.130 --> 01:23:19.440
I know the pain of losing someone.

01:23:19.440 --> 01:23:22.480
How could I have been so careless?

01:23:23.920 --> 01:23:25.180
Nee-san...

01:23:27.210 --> 01:23:29.730
\"E-Rantel - Communal Cemetery\"

01:23:45.700 --> 01:23:46.830
Here?

01:23:52.180 --> 01:23:53.510
I'm going in!

01:24:04.750 --> 01:24:07.650
Hey! I came to see Khaj-chan!

01:24:07.650 --> 01:24:08.880
Is he here?

01:24:10.650 --> 01:24:13.710
Could you stop saying hello like that?

01:24:13.710 --> 01:24:16.740
It's disrespectful towards Zurrernorn.

01:24:17.110 --> 01:24:20.680
Anyway, what do you want, Clementine?

01:24:21.760 --> 01:24:24.080
I brought this for you.

01:24:24.080 --> 01:24:28.080
That's... the Crown of Wisdom,
proof of the Miko Princess!

01:24:28.080 --> 01:24:31.690
It's one of the great treasures
of the Slane Theocracy!

01:24:31.690 --> 01:24:33.230
That's right.

01:24:33.230 --> 01:24:36.880
I stole it because a cute girl
was wearing this weird thing.

01:24:36.880 --> 01:24:40.100
She went completely insane when I stole it!

01:24:40.990 --> 01:24:43.970
You were a member of the Black Scripture.

01:24:43.970 --> 01:24:46.250
It seals the consciousness of the wearer,

01:24:46.250 --> 01:24:49.950
and instead turns them into
a powerful magical item.

01:24:49.950 --> 01:24:52.450
You knew very well what would happen to

01:24:52.450 --> 01:24:54.620
a Miko Princess if you
forcibly took it from her.

01:24:54.620 --> 01:24:56.570
Well, yeah.

01:24:56.570 --> 01:25:00.950
Besides, that item can only be
used by one in a million people.

01:25:00.950 --> 01:25:04.200
Without a suitable wearer,
it's nothing more than a piece of junk.

01:25:04.900 --> 01:25:10.330
That's why, seeing as I am part of Zurrernorn
as well, I was wondering if you could help me.

01:25:10.330 --> 01:25:12.040
Help you?

01:25:12.040 --> 01:25:16.900
I heard there's a talent who can
use any magic item in this town.

01:25:16.900 --> 01:25:20.180
Maybe that guy could use an item like this.

01:25:20.180 --> 01:25:24.610
If you want to kidnap someone,
why would you need my help?

01:25:24.610 --> 01:25:29.020
It's just that I kind of want to
make a big deal out of it for once!

01:25:29.020 --> 01:25:32.570
So you're going to use chaos to escape?

01:25:33.940 --> 01:25:36.740
I was just making the arrangements myself.

01:25:37.410 --> 01:25:39.490
The Spiral of Death, huh?

01:25:39.970 --> 01:25:41.110
That's right.

01:25:41.110 --> 01:25:46.640
I'm going to turn E-Rantel into
a city of undead using this.

01:25:46.640 --> 01:25:50.390
And I'll gather the overwhelming power
of death to carry out this ceremony.

01:25:50.390 --> 01:25:51.630
The Spiral of Death.

01:25:52.230 --> 01:25:56.510
And then I'll become immortal.

01:25:56.900 --> 01:26:00.890
So what if I helped you
achieve just that, Khaj-chan?

01:26:01.540 --> 01:26:03.710
Isn't that a good deal?

01:26:18.590 --> 01:26:19.860
I screwed up.

01:26:20.970 --> 01:26:26.950
Momon-san, I'm really sorry about last night.

01:26:29.920 --> 01:26:34.920
Even though I was transfigured into an undead
physically and mentally, I still feel emotions.

01:26:37.170 --> 01:26:39.780
Considering we're in such a pretty area,

01:26:39.780 --> 01:26:42.430
there's no need to be
walking in formation like this.

01:26:42.430 --> 01:26:44.310
It's important to be on guard!

01:26:44.310 --> 01:26:46.930
Indeed. Carelessness is an enemy itself.

01:26:46.930 --> 01:26:51.190
We might be suddenly attacked by a dragon.

01:26:51.190 --> 01:26:54.560
You really think something
like that can happen, Ninya?

01:26:54.930 --> 01:27:01.860
There's a legend that there used to be a
weather-controlling dragon around E-Rantel.

01:27:02.620 --> 01:27:11.000
Besides, the Azerlisha mountain range over
there is said to harbor several frost dragons.

01:27:14.550 --> 01:27:18.750
Do you know the name of the
weather-controlling dragon?

01:27:19.980 --> 01:27:21.910
Oh, I've never heard of its name.

01:27:21.910 --> 01:27:24.010
I'll look it up when we get back.

01:27:24.010 --> 01:27:27.430
Yes, I'm counting on you, Ninya-san.

01:27:28.440 --> 01:27:31.430
U-Understood, Momon-san!

01:27:33.520 --> 01:27:35.520
We're nearly at Carne Village.

01:27:38.540 --> 01:27:42.490
Dragons were the strongest
species in Yggdrasil as well.

01:27:42.490 --> 01:27:44.360
If they also exist in this world,

01:27:44.360 --> 01:27:46.280
I should watch out for them.

01:27:49.620 --> 01:27:51.800
Huh? That's strange.

01:27:51.800 --> 01:27:53.000
What's wrong?

01:27:53.490 --> 01:27:57.000
There wasn't a fence like that before.

01:27:59.800 --> 01:28:02.500
Hey. Call our Master, right now.

01:28:08.810 --> 01:28:10.890
Aren't those goblins?

01:28:11.480 --> 01:28:13.140
Who are you people?!

01:28:16.600 --> 01:28:19.150
First of all, put down your weapons.

01:28:19.800 --> 01:28:21.110
These guys are...

01:28:21.110 --> 01:28:26.610
Guys, we'd like to avoid
fighting as much as possible.

01:28:27.120 --> 01:28:29.730
Especially against the full plate armor guy.

01:28:29.730 --> 01:28:34.120
You're giving me a pretty bad feeling!

01:28:35.620 --> 01:28:37.460
What's wrong with these guys?!

01:28:37.460 --> 01:28:40.120
Goblin-san, what's wrong?

01:28:40.120 --> 01:28:40.800
Master!

01:28:41.460 --> 01:28:42.300
Enri!

01:28:44.230 --> 01:28:45.550
Nfirea!

01:28:45.930 --> 01:28:49.840
So these are the goblins she summoned
with the item I gave her back then.

01:28:50.750 --> 01:28:52.180
However...

01:28:52.610 --> 01:28:57.190
I have a pharmacist friend who visits
town occasionally, and he uses magic.

01:28:57.190 --> 01:28:57.860
- It's been a long time.

01:28:57.860 --> 01:28:58.570
- I never would've expected that to be him.
- It's been a long time.

01:28:58.570 --> 01:29:00.530
- I never would've expected that to be him.
- How are you?

01:29:02.830 --> 01:29:05.530
Well then, I'm going to
enter the forest from here,

01:29:05.530 --> 01:29:07.450
so I'm counting on you to guard me.

01:29:07.450 --> 01:29:11.240
I think we're going to be fine
as long as Momon-san is here.

01:29:11.680 --> 01:29:13.370
Um, Momon-san?

01:29:13.370 --> 01:29:15.500
If the Wise King of the Forest appears,

01:29:15.500 --> 01:29:18.500
could you chase it away without killing it?

01:29:18.950 --> 01:29:20.750
Why do you want that?

01:29:21.200 --> 01:29:24.720
The reason Carne Village hasn't
been attacked by monsters

01:29:24.720 --> 01:29:29.120
is because this is the Wise King's territory.

01:29:29.120 --> 01:29:31.390
So if you defeat him...

01:29:31.390 --> 01:29:33.840
That's impossible even for him, though.

01:29:33.840 --> 01:29:35.890
Understood.

01:29:35.890 --> 01:29:39.320
You're talking about a legendary creature
that has lived for hundreds of years!

01:29:39.320 --> 01:29:42.520
That's an attitude that only the
strongest can afford to have.

01:29:46.530 --> 01:29:49.030
Momon-san.

01:29:49.030 --> 01:29:50.680
Do you have a minute?

01:29:50.680 --> 01:29:51.780
What is it?

01:29:54.440 --> 01:29:56.540
Enri told me about it.

01:29:57.290 --> 01:30:01.040
A person named Ainz Ooal
Gown saved the village.

01:30:01.760 --> 01:30:06.050
And then her life was saved by a red potion.

01:30:07.540 --> 01:30:11.220
The red potion you gave to the girl at the inn

01:30:11.930 --> 01:30:15.470
isn't an item that you can create normally.

01:30:16.280 --> 01:30:19.480
And then the name Albedo...

01:30:20.130 --> 01:30:23.730
Are you Ainz Ooal Gown, Momon-san?!

01:30:25.280 --> 01:30:29.490
I'm sure you have a reason
for hiding your true name.

01:30:30.350 --> 01:30:35.620
I just wanted to thank you for saving Enri.

01:30:39.610 --> 01:30:40.870
Raise your head.

01:30:42.410 --> 01:30:46.740
I'm just a regular adventurer
named Momon right now.

01:30:46.740 --> 01:30:49.380
I'd be happy if you didn't forget that.

01:30:49.700 --> 01:30:52.660
Yes! I won't tell anybody about it!

01:30:54.870 --> 01:30:57.390
Ainz-sama, I am very sorry.

01:30:57.960 --> 01:30:59.480
Raise your head.

01:31:00.170 --> 01:31:03.900
If I'm not mistaken, you
did say Albedo's name.

01:31:04.710 --> 01:31:06.310
But that's alright.

01:31:06.310 --> 01:31:10.190
More importantly, there's
something we have to do right now.

01:31:10.190 --> 01:31:11.150
And that is?

01:31:11.570 --> 01:31:13.990
We're defeating the Wise King of the Forest.

01:31:14.950 --> 01:31:21.280
I already had Aura investigate where the
Wise King is hiding within this forest.

01:31:22.140 --> 01:31:25.130
It's all in order to spread my reputation.

01:31:27.760 --> 01:31:29.840
I kind of wanted to keep it,

01:31:29.840 --> 01:31:32.990
but it can't be helped, since
it's an order from Ainz-sama.

01:31:39.890 --> 01:31:42.140
Job completed!

01:31:51.420 --> 01:31:52.990
This is bad.

01:31:53.450 --> 01:31:55.880
Something huge is coming this way.

01:31:55.880 --> 01:31:57.450
The Wise King of the Forest?

01:31:58.530 --> 01:32:01.160
Leave the rest to us.

01:32:01.160 --> 01:32:02.200
Please do so!

01:32:02.200 --> 01:32:03.540
We're counting on you.

01:32:04.910 --> 01:32:06.310
Momon-san.

01:32:06.310 --> 01:32:07.670
Yes?

01:32:07.670 --> 01:32:09.920
Don't push yourself too much.

01:32:10.420 --> 01:32:12.800
Yes. Hurry up and get out of the forest.

01:32:14.890 --> 01:32:17.050
That's what I said,

01:32:17.570 --> 01:32:22.810
but there's no way to confirm that it was
the Wise King without any witnesses.

01:32:23.970 --> 01:32:26.940
Maybe I should cut off one or two of its legs?

01:32:28.310 --> 01:32:30.570
Our guest is here.

01:32:57.010 --> 01:32:59.680
You were able to completely
block my first attack.

01:32:59.680 --> 01:33:00.850
Commendable.

01:33:01.520 --> 01:33:02.850
A monkey?

01:33:03.210 --> 01:33:06.810
Well then, newcomers.

01:33:06.810 --> 01:33:08.920
If you retreat right now,

01:33:08.920 --> 01:33:13.220
I will not chase you out of respect
for your commendable act.

01:33:13.220 --> 01:33:14.610
What are you going to do, then?

01:33:14.610 --> 01:33:16.260
How foolish.

01:33:16.260 --> 01:33:19.730
Aren't you hiding yourself
because you're insecure?

01:33:19.730 --> 01:33:22.280
Or are you just shy?

01:33:22.280 --> 01:33:24.380
How arrogant.

01:33:24.380 --> 01:33:28.750
Well then, you may tremble
in fear at this imposing sight!

01:33:42.250 --> 01:33:43.560
I can't believe it!

01:33:45.120 --> 01:33:49.350
I can feel your dismay and
fear from below your helmet.

01:33:50.120 --> 01:33:52.230
I'd like to ask you something.

01:33:52.230 --> 01:33:57.360
Isn't your species called
the Djungarian Hamster?

01:33:58.610 --> 01:33:59.680
What?!

01:33:59.680 --> 01:34:03.370
You know about my species?

01:34:03.370 --> 01:34:04.750
Y-Yes.

01:34:04.750 --> 01:34:07.110
I guess you could say I know about it.

01:34:07.110 --> 01:34:11.040
One of my friends from long ago
had a pet that looked just like you.

01:34:11.830 --> 01:34:13.070
What?!

01:34:13.070 --> 01:34:16.420
I'd like to know if there are
others of the same species.

01:34:16.730 --> 01:34:20.880
If I can't breed any offspring,
I'd be failing as a living creature.

01:34:20.880 --> 01:34:24.120
Well, that would be impossible
because of your size.

01:34:24.120 --> 01:34:26.320
I see.

01:34:26.320 --> 01:34:27.920
What a shame.

01:34:27.920 --> 01:34:29.060
Sorry.

01:34:29.940 --> 01:34:31.570
It's okay.

01:34:31.570 --> 01:34:33.240
More importantly,

01:34:33.240 --> 01:34:38.320
shall we stop the useless
chit-chat and duel to the death?

01:34:38.720 --> 01:34:40.410
Nabe, stand back.

01:34:40.410 --> 01:34:43.400
I don't mind if I'm outnumbered by you two.

01:34:43.400 --> 01:34:47.850
I can't do something as embarrassing
as fighting a hamster two-on-one.

01:34:47.850 --> 01:34:49.910
Well then, here I go!

01:34:51.940 --> 01:34:52.920
Take this!

01:34:57.230 --> 01:34:59.670
Commendable.

01:35:01.460 --> 01:35:03.470
You can use magic, too?

01:35:03.810 --> 01:35:07.780
Low tier magic and mental
magic has no effect on me.

01:35:12.820 --> 01:35:15.360
That's not thick fur?

01:35:15.360 --> 01:35:16.490
In that case!

01:35:24.980 --> 01:35:27.580
Now, we are square.

01:35:28.080 --> 01:35:29.740
You have done well.

01:35:29.740 --> 01:35:32.330
You're a respectable warrior.

01:35:32.330 --> 01:35:33.960
Warrior?

01:35:33.960 --> 01:35:36.710
Or maybe you're a knight?

01:35:37.680 --> 01:35:40.720
I don't want you seeing that I'm an undead...

01:35:44.570 --> 01:35:48.190
Maybe it's because of the
Wise King of the Forest name,

01:35:48.190 --> 01:35:49.820
but I had high expectations.

01:35:49.820 --> 01:35:50.850
How disappointing.

01:35:51.520 --> 01:35:54.100
A complete letdown.

01:35:54.100 --> 01:35:56.610
What are you doing?

01:35:56.610 --> 01:36:02.490
I refuse to believe that you're surrendering
before there is a clear winner!

01:36:02.490 --> 01:36:06.320
Alright, we're fighting for real now!

01:36:06.320 --> 01:36:08.420
We're fighting to the death!

01:36:08.420 --> 01:36:10.940
I give up.

01:36:12.090 --> 01:36:15.260
Skill: Aura of Despair!

01:36:16.960 --> 01:36:18.990
Level one!

01:36:27.890 --> 01:36:29.920
I surrender!

01:36:29.920 --> 01:36:32.390
It's my loss.

01:36:33.350 --> 01:36:35.130
He's just a beast, after all.

01:36:35.130 --> 01:36:37.060
You're going to kill him?

01:36:37.060 --> 01:36:40.230
In that case, I'd like to keep his fur.

01:36:40.230 --> 01:36:42.400
I think it would make a nice dress.

01:36:42.400 --> 01:36:45.380
N-No way!

01:36:46.160 --> 01:36:49.200
This is... the Wise King of the Forest?

01:36:49.580 --> 01:36:51.640
Don't worry about him.

01:36:51.640 --> 01:36:54.120
He's completely under my control,

01:36:54.120 --> 01:36:57.050
so he won't rampage at all.

01:36:57.050 --> 01:36:59.630
It's just as my master says.

01:36:59.630 --> 01:37:04.190
I'm going to guide my master through
the forest and serve as his guide!

01:37:04.190 --> 01:37:08.240
I won't be causing any trouble to any of you.

01:37:08.240 --> 01:37:09.430
Amazing!

01:37:09.430 --> 01:37:11.180
What a wonderful magical beast!

01:37:12.050 --> 01:37:15.180
I can feel great strength and
wisdom coming from it!

01:37:15.180 --> 01:37:16.550
Great strength?

01:37:16.550 --> 01:37:17.560
Wisdom?

01:37:17.560 --> 01:37:19.770
You've accomplished many feats.

01:37:19.770 --> 01:37:23.030
I can see that Nabe-chan was a great help!

01:37:23.030 --> 01:37:26.010
We would have been completely massacred.

01:37:26.010 --> 01:37:27.410
As expected of Momon-san.

01:37:27.410 --> 01:37:29.170
You're incredible!

01:37:29.170 --> 01:37:31.170
What do you think, Nabe?

01:37:31.170 --> 01:37:35.710
Leaving its strength aside,
his eyes look powerful.

01:37:36.400 --> 01:37:38.210
No way!

01:37:40.650 --> 01:37:41.960
Well then, Momon-san.

01:37:42.280 --> 01:37:47.600
We'll get going to Nfirea-san's place
to drop him off and call it a day.

01:37:47.600 --> 01:37:48.910
Understood.

01:37:48.910 --> 01:37:52.970
I will go and register this magical
creature and get going as well.

01:37:52.970 --> 01:37:55.910
I was able to collect a lot today
thanks to you, Momon-san!

01:37:55.910 --> 01:37:57.980
I'll prepare a bonus payment for you.

01:37:57.980 --> 01:38:01.390
- I also helped you out with
the herb gathering, though—

01:38:01.390 --> 01:38:02.730
- Well then!
- I also helped you out with
the herb gathering, though—

01:38:03.140 --> 01:38:06.930
Nabe-chan, though it's just for a short
time, don't get lonely without me!

01:38:06.930 --> 01:38:09.090
I'll make sure to party with you later!

01:38:09.090 --> 01:38:11.120
Water flea. I'll stomp you.

01:38:11.120 --> 01:38:12.610
Let's get going already.

01:38:12.610 --> 01:38:14.120
See you later.

01:38:16.990 --> 01:38:19.120
Is this something to be proud of?

01:38:19.880 --> 01:38:23.630
I feel like an old man
riding a merry-go-round.

01:38:23.630 --> 01:38:25.630
This is so embarrassing!

01:38:25.630 --> 01:38:27.280
Damn it!

01:38:27.280 --> 01:38:30.630
Ah, I guess I have to give this guy a name.

01:38:30.630 --> 01:38:31.690
Hamsuke!

01:38:31.690 --> 01:38:33.890
Or maybe I should go with Daifuku?

01:38:40.850 --> 01:38:43.770
Everyone. Could you help
me carry them over here?

01:38:43.770 --> 01:38:45.650
Alright!

01:38:46.070 --> 01:38:48.320
Grandma isn't home?

01:38:54.160 --> 01:38:57.290
Hi! Welcome back.
